{"raw": {"https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/post-doctoral-research-position-hybrid-flexible-work-arrangement-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Post-Doctoral Research Position", "description": "Post-Doctoral Research Position - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Post-Doctoral Research Position - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Post-Doctoral Research Position 507437 Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions Full-Time Closing on: Nov 19 2026 Job Summary Drs. de Marchena and Wieckowski from the A.J. Drexel Autism Institute are recruiting for a postdoctoral fellow for three ongoing NIH-funded grants, to conduct autism research. Study foci include measuring communication for autistic adults as well as investigating a tiered approach for autism diagnosis in toddlers. Candidates will be working at the Drexel Autism Institute, which is a multidisciplinary institute emphasizing public health science approaches. Candidates will lead, design, develop, conduct, and communicate research often with a wide range of collaborators. They will receive mentoring on research with an emphasis on autism intervention, social networks and communication supports. Independence to pursue their own lines of research/ service/ learning/ outreach/ teaching will be encouraged. This position is grant-funded; employment is contingent upon the continued availability of those funds. Essential Functions Lead and coordinate research activities associated with NIH-funded projects in autism and other communication and developmental disorders. Mentor graduate and undergraduate students in experimental design, laboratory techniques, data analysis, and scientific communication. Lead and contribute to manuscripts, presentations, progress reports, and future grant applications. Promote rigorous experimental practices, clear documentation, and an organized and collaborative laboratory environment Perform or oversee autism evaluations and other clinical work required of the different studies. Coordinate with collaborators and project personnel to help maintain progress toward project milestones. Use Sharepoint, maintain meticulous and well-organized records (i.e. recording notes for all meetings in notebook, completing all tracking information for project implementation, engaging in timely internal and external communications, project management (creating detailed project SOPs), and all other aspects of the job. Contribute to the intellectual environment of the institute Practice outstanding written and oral communication abilities Required Qualifications Minimum of a PhD or Doctorate in Minimum of a PhD or Doctorate in psychology, social work. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 5-8 years of research experience. Research experience in autism, developmental disabilities, and other communication disorders Strong experimental, analytical, and scientific communication skills. Strong organizational skills and attention to experimental documentation and laboratory operations. Experience working both independently and under direction Expertise in community-engaged research Some experience with autism intervention and qualitative and quantitative social network research Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated capability in intervention science, demonstrated scientific writing skills, and successful ability to pursue funding Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Location Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade K . Compensation for this grade ranges from $60,240 to $90350 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 34395b66 Last Name (required) dbbf82af Email (required) b260a2d5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Athletics, Drexel University Athletics is seeking an Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 2b6362f3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Nursing and Health Professions College of Nursing and Health Professions Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) eca190de Last Name (required) 27dcf746 Email (required) 0485d09e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/executive-director-of-marketing-and-communications-hybrid-flexible-work-arrangement-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Executive Director of Marketing and Communications", "description": "Executive Director of Marketing and Communications - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Executive Director of Marketing and Communications - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Executive Director of Marketing and Communications 507434 Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University Kline School of Law Full-Time Closing on: Nov 16 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Executive Director of Marketing and Communications is a senior strategic leader who sets the vision and leads execution of an integrated marketing and communications program for the Thomas R. Kline School of Law. Reporting to the Dean, the Executive Director unifies brand, recruitment, and reputation-building efforts to elevate the Law School\u2019s visibility and impact, regionally and nationally, among prospective students, faculty, alumni, the legal profession, and the public. In partnership with Admissions, Experiential Learning, Career Strategies, faculty, the Dean\u2019s Office, University Marketing & Communications, and Institutional Advancement, the Executive Director designs strategies that support enrollment across the JD, LLM, MLS, and undergraduate programs and advance the Law School\u2019s reputation for scholarship, experiential learning, bar passage, and graduate employment. The Executive Director leads the marketing and communications team \u2014 including the Director of Communications & Digital Strategy and Creative Director \u2014 serving as the Law School\u2019s brand and content strategist and owning the department\u2019s budget and technology investments. A central responsibility is identifying and telling the stories that distinguish the Law School: the Executive Director is a skilled, hands-on writer and editor who can translate scholarship, student and alumni achievement, and institutional priorities into compelling content for varied audiences. Writing will be an important responsibility of the Executive Director. The successful candidate is an experienced leader and a creative, outcome-driven strategist who thrives in a fast-paced academic environment, bringing intellectual curiosity, sound judgment, and a data-informed approach to continuous improvement. This position is hybrid, requiring the Executive Director to report to work in the office 4 days a week, and permitting remote work 1 day a week. Essential Functions Strategic Leadership & Vision: Develop and lead execution of the Law School\u2019s marketing and communications strategic plan, establishing performance goals and KPIs that guide resource allocation and continuous improvement. Support achievement of annual enrollment, alumni engagement, and reputation goals through coordinated marketing strategies that build visibility, reputation, and rankings, internally and externally. Brand & Creative Strategy: Serve as the Law School\u2019s brand and creative strategist, setting brand voice, visual identity, and creative direction, and advancing a differentiated brand narrative that highlights faculty scholarship, experiential and clinical programs, and student and alumni outcomes. Oversee website strategy, information architecture, and digital content plans, ensuring the Law School\u2019s digital presence is cohesive and on-brand. Content Strategy & Production: Own editorial and content strategy and standards across the Law School\u2019s digital and print platforms, including admissions, recruitment, and alumni communications. Identify and produce the stories, publications, viewbooks, and annual reports that advance the Law School\u2019s reputation; determine staffing and resourcing needs for content production. Team Building & Operational Management: Build and lead a collaborative, high-performing team, defining roles and responsibilities and supporting staff onboarding and professional development. Develop, manage, and monitor the annual marketing and communications budget. Establish spending priorities, and evaluate return on investment, vendor relationships, and contracts. Maintain strong relationships with University Marketing & Communications and other central offices, advising Law School leadership on University brand platforms and policies. Recruitment Marketing & Enrollment Support: In partnership with relevant Law School stakeholders and enrollment management vendors, lead performance-based recruitment marketing and yield strategy across all Law School programs. Oversee digital advertising, paid search, CRM automation, and social media targeting, coordinating on SEO and organic web performance. Stakeholder Engagement & Reputation Building: Strengthen the Law School\u2019s visibility and reputation among alumni, donors, the bench and bar, legal employers, rankings bodies, and academic peers, serving as primary liaison to the University\u2019s communications team on earned media opportunities. Collaborate with Institutional Advancement on alumni engagement campaigns, and lead and coordinate crisis, strategic, and executive communications with the Dean, senior leadership, and University Marketing & Communications. Other duties as assigned. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree in Marketing, Communications, Public Relations, Journalism, or a related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience. or the equivalent combination of education and work experience ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information). Minimum of 8 years of communications and marketing experience, including at least 3 years in a management-level role. Exceptional writing and editing skills, able to translate complex content into clear, compelling messages. Proven experience planning and executing integrated communications strategies, including digital marketing, across web, social, and print channels. Strong project management skills and a track record of engaging diverse teams and stakeholders. Experience with CRM platforms (e.g., Slate, Salesforce), digital analytics, and marketing automation tools, and a demonstrated ability to connect performance metrics to outcomes. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Marketing, Communications, Journalism, or a related field. Experience in higher education marketing, ideally within a law school or other professional/graduate program. Knowledge of the legal education marketplace and experience in enrollment marketing. Documented success leading significant communications and marketing initiatives, with expertise in brand strategy and paid advertising. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Location Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade O . Compensation for this grade ranges from $119,470.00 - $179,200.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. #LI-Hybrid Apply Now First Name (required) 5e3020c1 Last Name (required) f72ccd4e Email (required) 7907367c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Athletics, Drexel University Athletics is seeking an Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming Sign up for job alerts Job Alert ee6b6691 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Kline School of Law Drexel University Kline School of Law Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 73f5185d Last Name (required) 1517a696 Email (required) f022163d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/licensing-manager-remote-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Licensing Manager", "description": "Licensing Manager - Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Licensing Manager - Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Licensing Manager 507418 Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation Full-Time Closing on: Nov 16 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Office of Applied Innovation is seeking to hire a Licensing Manager. Drexel Applied Innovation, a unit within Drexel University\u2019s Office of Research & Innovation, expands the impact of Drexel research through technology transfer. The team focuses on two core functions: Intellectual Property & Agreements, and Industry Engagement. Applied Innovation is also responsible for playing a leadership role in elevating the University\u2019s innovation ecosystem by collaborating with a variety of university-wide initiatives and stakeholders to support Drexel innovators, such as entrepreneurial and translational research programs. At the direction of and under the supervision of the Director of IP & Agreements, this position will focus on technologies in life sciences and engineering/tech disciplines and be part of a multidisciplinary team covering the breadth of Drexel\u2019s research expertise. Essential Functions Essential Functions As a member of the Intellectual Property (IP) & Agreements team, the Licensing Manager will: Evaluate Drexel inventions and discoveries for potential protection. Protect qualifying Drexel discoveries and innovation through patents, copyrights, trademarks, and trade secrets. Develop supportive relationships and contribute to timely and high-quality contracts and agreements to support tech transfer and industry sponsored research. Relationship building and Customer Service. Connect and collaborate with faculty, professional and administrative staff, outside service providers, companies, investors, and entrepreneurs. Assess and commercialize inventions: Identify research programs and discoveries with commercial potential. Drive the process for analyzing the commercial potential of Drexel technologies, developing, and executing commercialization strategies, and execute marketing and business development efforts. Review and negotiate agreements: Draft and complete term sheets, confidentiality agreements, options, licenses and inter-institutional agreements, memoranda of understanding, material transfer agreements and other agreements and contracts necessary in the licensing process. Education and training: As a member of Drexel Applied Innovation, educate the Drexel community about Drexel Applied Innovation services and promote the culture of innovation. Hybrid work. Primarily Remote, with some time required on campus/at events. Other related duties as assigned by Director, IP & Agreements and Asst Vice Provost, Applied Innovation. Required Qualifications Minimum of a master's degree in engineering, life sciences, or biomedical engineering discipline or an equivalent combination of education and experience or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information). Minimum of At least 3 years related experience in technology commercialization. Experience in managing a large, diverse set of tasks and projects. Knowledge of disciplines relevant to the university\u2019s programs in life sciences, engineering/technology or biomedical engineering. Must process excellent analytical and negotiating skills. Excellent time management and prioritization skills. Excellent verbal and written communication. Independent self-starter and strong work ethic. Good attention to details, follow through and closing. Availability to work on campus and attend campus/Philadelphia innovation ecosystem events, as occasionally required. Preferred Qualifications PhD in engineering, life sciences, or biomedical engineering discipline or an equivalent combination of education. Experience in academic technology transfer. Experience in corporate or academic business development. Evidence of creative problem-solving, entrepreneurship, initiative, and intellectual curiosity. Demonstrated ability to work energetically and produce results. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Lifting demands \u2264 25lbs Location Remote Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade N . Compensation for this grade ranges from $99,720.00 - $149,580.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. #LI-Remote Apply Now First Name (required) 922f6998 Last Name (required) 979d04a1 Email (required) 635137fc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Athletics, Drexel University Athletics is seeking an Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming Sign up for job alerts Job Alert d3d64674 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Office of Research & Innovation Office of Research & Innovation Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Remote, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) eb5d8543 Last Name (required) a0ef26dc Email (required) 0a556aca Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/assistant-coach-men-s-and-women-s-swimming-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming - University City", "description": "Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Assistant Coach, Men's and Women's Swimming 507380 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Athletics Drexel University Full-Time Closing on: Nov 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Assistant Swim Coach is responsible for teaching athletic skills, strategies and techniques in the sport and mentor the student athletes by utilizing coaching methodologies in a competitive sport environment and fostering academic achievement of the student. This is a full-time position. Essential Functions Assists in planning, critiquing and implementing strategies designed to achieve success in a competitive sports program by breaking down and analyzing trends and strategies; making recommendations for new strategies. Develops the student athlete's skills and performance during sports competition on the Division 1 level by teaching new strategies and techniques, providing detailed game plans; implementing and conducting training programs. Assists with the preparation and implementation of weekly practice and conditioning sessions. Monitors students' adherence to department, conference and NCAA guidelines, resolving issues and reporting infractions. Identifies and recruits student athletes who are qualified to compete academically and athletically at the Division I level by analyzing and evaluating the skill level of potential recruits. Analyzes and evaluates the academic potential of new recruits; assessing the needs of the program and the available options to fulfill individual personal needs. Functions as a mentor and liaison with the Athletic Academic Office (Achieve Center) by working with assigned student athletes to assure proper academic progress is achieved according to the University Conference and NCAA guidelines; acts as the liaison with the office regarding the progress of assigned student athletes; serves as a resource for personal issues such as nutrition, social, and family issues. Assists with daily operations and management by preparing and maintaining proper documentation on NCAA related matters to ensure compliance on issues such as recruiting, official visits and practice schedules. Performs other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 2 years of experience. Valid Driver's License. Knowledge of teaching and coaching skills in sport. Knowledge of all aspects of the sport. Knowledge of basic counseling techniques. Knowledge of NCAA guidelines. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work evenings and weekends. Ability to travel as needed. Preferred Qualifications Previous collegiate coaching experience. Knowledge of NCAA and conference rules. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Typically running, climbing Lifting demands \u2264 50lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt. Compensation for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 33dc063e Last Name (required) be319345 Email (required) 360866ef Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 275c89ff Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Athletics Drexel University Athletics Drexel University Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 3c1ced41 Last Name (required) 9b013abf Email (required) 30c4d11d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/mechanic-class-a-electrician-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Mechanic Class A - Electrician - University City", "description": "Mechanic Class A - Electrician - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Mechanic Class A - Electrician - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Mechanic Class A - Electrician 507316 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Drexel University Finance and Administration Full-Time Closing on: Nov 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Drexel University's Facilities Management Department is seeking a qualified candidate to serve as a Union Electrician / Multi-skilled Maintenance employee. This position is Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. Essential Functions General maintenance, repair, and installation of electrical equipment, including sub-panels, wiring, circuit breakers, and conduit installation. Replace fluorescent ballasts and tubes. Respond to service calls for general building maintenance items campus-wide which will include work in classrooms, restrooms and occasionally residence halls, athletic facilities and outdoor work. Maintaining indoor and exterior lighting and LED components and upgrades. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a HS Diploma or GED. Minimum of 3 years of relevant experience, including: proficiency in working on 120V-480V single-phase and three-phase systems. ability to wire sub-panels, motors, and other electrical equipment. Philadelphia electrical contractors license or equivalent license. Candidate must possess a valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications The job requires an employee who can perform with minimum supervision and take the initiative to complete the assignment. Minimum experience of three to five years preferred. Physical Demands Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 50lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This is a Full-Time Union position classified as Non-Exempt. Benefits and compensation are based on the agreed Collective Bargaining Agreement for this position. Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 30b54dd3 Last Name (required) c77620b1 Email (required) d7cd4c5d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e1cac059 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Finance and Administration Drexel University Finance and Administration Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 7d1f51ff Last Name (required) 287846cc Email (required) fdfce6bb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/healthcare-compliance-specialist-hybrid-flexible-work-arrangement-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Healthcare Compliance Specialist", "description": "Healthcare Compliance Specialist - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Healthcare Compliance Specialist - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Healthcare Compliance Specialist 507321 Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University Finance and Administration Full-Time Closing on: Nov 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The primary role of the Healthcare Compliance Specialist is to support the operational functions of Compliance Program Services by providing healthcare monitoring and education services for Drexel University clinical practices. The Healthcare Compliance Specialist is a regulatory expert who helps educate and advise the University toward excellence in healthcare compliance. The Healthcare Compliance Specialist reports to the Director, Compliance Program Services. Essential Functions Oversee the University\u2019s health care compliance program. Serve as primary liaison between Compliance Program Services and Drexel clinical directors and administrative leadership. Research and analyze current Medicare and Medicaid regulations applicable to the University. Maintain comprehensive knowledge of billing, reimbursement, and coding guidelines. Perform Coding and Billing audits for Drexel Health clinical practices. Provide education and training to Physicians and clinicians to remediate audit findings and manage risk. Develop and update healthcare compliance policies and procedures, as required. Perform and review monthly screening processes against federal and state sanction databases, ensuring system confirmations and associated follow ups, as necessary. Oversee and ensure completion of annual healthcare trainings required by Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services. Complete and assure annual First Tier, Downstream or Related entity (FDR) attestations required by Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services. Perform other duties as assigned by Director, Compliance Program Services and/or the Chief Compliance Officer. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a HS Diploma or GED Minimum of 3-5 years combined experience in medical auditing, academic medicine compliance, medical coding, office professional fee coding, and reimbursement. Certified Professional Medical Auditor (CPMA). Physician coding certification (CPC or CCS-P). Exceptional ability to formulate compliance policies, procedures, and related documentation. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills. Expert spreadsheet and database management skills. Verifiable ability to maintain the highest level of diplomacy and confidentiality. Preferred Qualifications Certified in Healthcare Compliance (CHC). Experience working in higher education and/or a complex organization a plus. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in teams and groups to plan, implement, and influence organizational change. Location Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade J. Compensation for this grade ranges from $ 52,360.00 to $ 78,530.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. #LI-Hybrid Apply Now First Name (required) 528910e5 Last Name (required) da30584b Email (required) 4ed6abd9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 1ddc691f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Finance and Administration Drexel University Finance and Administration Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) b07383b2 Last Name (required) 01996951 Email (required) e6f09da3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/research-clinical-nurse-specialist-center-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Research Clinical Nurse Specialist - Center City", "description": "Research Clinical Nurse Specialist - Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Research Clinical Nurse Specialist - Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Research Clinical Nurse Specialist 507064 Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Medicine Part-Time Closing on: Nov 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary This position will provide clinical research support services to researchers within the assigned departments. This individual will support such researchers providing the required elements necessary to retain regulatory, clinical and ethical compliance with all aspects of the clinical trial process. In addition, this position will assist in providing research training for Drexel University clinical research, including Good Clinical Practices (GCP), at designated departments and facilities. Essential Functions Conducts full CNS and research duties for assigned trials including Regulatory, IRB, and Study Start up and close out activities, staff training, recruitment, and retention of study subjects as noted below: Promptly documents and reports any observed protocol/trial issues to the IRB, Research Administrator and PI. Ensures established procedures are followed in reviewing the collection of clinical data and the administration of clinical trials. Prepares and submits IRB documents under the direction of the Principal Investigator (PI), Research Administrator and prepares study related regulatory documents; Assists in development of contracts and budgets under direction of PI and Research Administrator. Review and ascertain invoice accuracy before remittance. Coordinates and participates in the pre-site, site initiation and interval monitoring visits. Remain 100% audit ready. Conducts trial search and feasibility in collaboration with PI. Participates in Investigator Meetings requiring some travel. Coordinates study initiation and assists with planning and design of source documents for protocol; adhering to study protocol Supports ongoing recruitment of volunteer subjects for clinical research; screens subjects for protocol eligibility and participation; and monitors enrollment goals. Provide participant compensation and/or stipends via clinical conductor. Ensures human subject safety. Maintain screening and enrollment logs and communicate results to PI. Organizes and facilitates with the PI- Subject Informed Consent from study participant and documents appropriately. Completes an initial subject assessment and ongoing assessments as per protocol utilizing interview, observation, and Physical Assessment skills. Obtains Vital Signs and performs phlebotomy, IV infusion, ECG, and other tests where applicable; some tests and procedures may require training specific to an individual study. Administers study drug and/or Investigational Product as per protocol. Monitors participants\u2019 labs and communicates results to PI in a timely manner; utilizing proper procedures, prepares and ships lab specimens as needed. Maintain laboratory logs and safety compliance including temperature and centrifuge records. Monitors and completes accurate source documentation and electronic Data capture as per protocol on all participant records, drug accountability, test devices and clinical supplies. Completes all required trainings for Sponsor\u2019s, Drexel and Hospital Electronic Data Capture and EMR. Utilizes data resources external to research area, as well as develops and facilitates productive working relationship with the study monitor, ancillary personnel, PI, study staff and clinical staff. As able, will supervise and assist in the development and education of new coordinators, research staff and physicians involved in clinical research. Maintain CITI training and certification. Resource Management: Demonstrates the ability to plan effectively by recognizing and setting priorities and completing assignments in a timely manner. Organizes work effectively, adjusts well to changes in work schedule, workflow, and priorities Seeks to utilize equipment, time, supplies, phones and other clinical research resources properly and efficiently Quality and Teamwork Operates in a collaborative manner and is open and flexible to the ideas of others. Seeks to provide the highest quality service in an accurate, thorough, and timely manner. Consistently adheres to Drexel University and department policies, procedures and standards regarding conduct, attendance, tardiness and appearance. Communication: Communicates (verbally and in writing) clearly, accurately and effectively. Initiative: Volunteers assistance to others, seeks additional assignments when work is completed, is flexible and willingly accepts additional responsibilities. Initiative: Makes all reasonable attempts to solve problems independently before turning them over to the supervisor with resolution proposal. Judgment/Decision Making: Exhibits sound judgment and makes appropriate decisions in a timely manner. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree in Nursing or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 3 years of experience. Graduation from an approved school of professional nursing, with BSN minimum degree, and licensed by the State of Pennsylvania as a registered nurse, 3 years of nursing experience preferred. Experience working in a clinical research environment, inpatient and/or outpatient settings Knowledge of Good Clinical practices Knowledge of FDA regulations Excellent organization skills are essential Confident computer skills Expert clinical skills, including, but not limited to Nursing Assessment skills, venipuncture, documentation of assessment and adverse events (AE\u2019s), medical history. Current Basic Life Support/CPR and/or Advanced Life Support Certification Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Location Center City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade L. Compensation for this grade ranges from $69,070 to $103,600 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) a066ec18 Last Name (required) aeafb7be Email (required) 0daa21df Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 115fe613 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Medicine College of Medicine Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 65fecf42 Last Name (required) 92feba14 Email (required) 35f2dc04 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/research-administrator-coordinator-remote-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Research Administrator Coordinator", "description": "Research Administrator Coordinator - Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Research Administrator Coordinator - Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Research Administrator Coordinator 507396 Remote, Pennsylvania Drexel University Office of Research & Innovation Full-Time Closing on: Nov 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Research Administrator Coordinator provides administrative and operational support for pre-award and post-award research administration activities within the Central Office of Sponsored Programs. This position serves as a key point of contact for faculty, departmental administrators, sponsors, and institutional stakeholders, facilitating the efficient processing of research proposals, agreements, and awards. The Coordinator is responsible for managing centralized communications, maintaining records, supporting workflow processes, and ensuring timely responses for research administration actions. Essential Functions Shared Mailbox Management: Monitor and manage the Sponsored Programs shared mailboxes to ensure timely review, triage, and distribution of incoming communications. Monitor, triage, and assign Novelution actions from faculty and departmental administrators to appropriate team members Respond to routine inquiries from faculty, research staff, departmental administrators, and external sponsors. Route requests, agreements, and related communications to appropriate Office of Sponsored Programs team members. Track and prioritize mailbox requests to ensure adherence to internal service standards and proposal deadlines. Maintain records of inquiries and resolutions to support customer service and process improvement efforts. Develop and maintain standardized email templates, FAQs, and communication resources. Research Administration Support: Coordinate communication between principal investigators, departments, schools, and central administrative offices. Assist in monitoring proposal and award activity and preparing reports as requested. Customer Service and Communication: Serve as a central point of contact for routine sponsored programs inquiries. Provide guidance regarding institutional processes, deadlines, and required documentation. Communicate effectively with faculty, research administrators, sponsors, and institutional partners. Escalate complex issues to appropriate research administration staff and leadership. Reporting and Administrative Operations: Support data entry, quality assurance, and record management activities. Assist with special projects and office-wide initiatives as assigned. Participate in training and continuous improvement efforts. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 1-3 years of experience. One to three years of administrative, research administration, grants management, or higher education experience. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Excel, Word, and Teams. Understanding of the role and function of research in a university setting Key Competencies Customer service orientation. Effective communication. Organizational and time management skills. Attention to detail. Problem-solving and critical thinking. Collaboration and teamwork. Confidentiality and professionalism. Ability to manage high-volume email and workflow operations. Preferred Qualifications Experience in sponsored programs, grants administration, or research administration. Experience with SmartSheet. Experience with customer-focused ticketing systems. Familiarity with electronic research administration systems (eRA). Experience managing shared mailboxes and service-oriented workflows. Knowledge of federal, state, foundation, and industry-sponsored research processes. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Lifting demands \u2264 25lbs Location Remote Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade J . Compensation for this grade ranges from $52,360.00 - $78,530.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. #LI-Remote Apply Now First Name (required) bca78c77 Last Name (required) 5a6d1cdb Email (required) 769b560f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert bd7d01ce Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Office of Research & Innovation Drexel University Office of Research & Innovation Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Remote, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 91517000 Last Name (required) 342a3b56 Email (required) 32057994 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/academic-advisor-salus-campus-elkins-park-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Academic Advisor - Salus Campus", "description": "Academic Advisor - Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Academic Advisor - Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Academic Advisor 507415 Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions Full-Time Closing on: Nov 14 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Academic Advisor (AA) is the forward-facing, single point of contact, and most significant advocate for Drexel students. The AA supports students throughout their academic lifespan, acceptance/confirmation until graduation, with a comprehensive approach to the student experience. The Academic Advisor assists students in navigating their way through the policies and resources of Drexel University to complete their degree or certificate program. The AA sustains proactive, consistent, timely, and respectful communication with students. The AA acts in the students' best interest and provides them with all relevant information, options, and resources. Essential Functions Student Success & Development Initiate and maintain consistent communication with assigned students multiple times per term Document and track student encounters and communications in advising software (AVT) Coordinate plan of study, assist with course registration and monitor academic progress Notify students of important dates & critical information such as add/drop deadlines, course registration timelines, clinical scheduling, course offerings, policy changes, etc. Provide students with all necessary information and potential options to make well-informed decisions about their academic career Create and update student plan of study and course sequencing - DegreeWorks if applicable Counsel and assist students with Web-registration Act as a liaison and refer assigned students to other University offices and resources (Drexel Central-financial aid) Track student progression and academic program requirements Troubleshoot student issues (e.g. life situations) and lead students to appropriate professionals/departments Liaison to faculty and administration on behalf of the student (acting as the single point of contact) Retention Improve positive student experiences, build and maintain positive relationships and acts as their advocate Identify students at risk academically to ensure resources are provided, and meet to identify their needs Proactive communication to all assigned students Identify obstacles for \u2018unregistered-eligible-to-enroll\u2019 students to improve term-over-term retention and decrease average time to completion Counsel students on best practices, time management techniques, and effective study methods Provide students with all resources throughout the college and University to address their needs, personal or academic Work with students to preserve their academic standing whenever possible Teach University 101 (if applicable) Recruitment - Prospective Students Participate in student recruitment events as needed Maintain and provide students with pre-approve external courses for transfer credit or pre-requisite requirements Work closely with the Enrollment Counselors/Admissions Coordinators to smoothly transition students from acceptance to enrollment/registration Orient students and ensure academic program expectations are understood Acts as the point person for accepted students with program/department specific questions Other Duties as Assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree in Education or a related field or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 2+ years of experience. Experience in higher education, working knowledge of academic programs/degrees Excellent interpersonal, written and oral communication skills Proficient with Microsoft Office products is required; experience with Banner, Hyperion or other higher education systems is beneficial Ability to maintain the confidentiality of student records and adhere to FERPA and other University policies related to student privacy Strong organizational & project management skills, superior attention to detail Excellent customer service & helpful demeanor Demonstrated success in finding appropriate solutions and taking initiative. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrate competence in working with diverse student populations Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Location Salus Campus - Elkins Park Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade I . Compensation for this grade ranges from $45,330 to $68,000 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) a2f724d3 Last Name (required) 4904e220 Email (required) 435338e9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert da215715 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Nursing and Health Professions College of Nursing and Health Professions Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 00f8a11b Last Name (required) 166a39d6 Email (required) dd5ab76a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/research-assistant-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states-e1f03ef7-5ca3-4585-b691-8efbdff6debb": {"title": "Research Assistant - University City", "description": "Research Assistant - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Research Assistant - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Research Assistant 507420 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions Full-Time Closing on: Nov 24 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Dr. Safiyyah Okoye and Dr. Alex Ezeh are seeking a research assistant to support projects related to health, physical function, and well-being of low-income older adults and their family caregivers, as well as global population change. This role will serve both Dr. Okoye\u2019s lab and Dr. Ezeh\u2019s Office of Global Health, with approximately 50% (20 hours/week) commitments to each. Dr. Okoye\u2019s academic mission is to conduct high quality, innovative research that generates knowledge and solutions related to improving the health and well-being of socioeconomically disadvantaged older adults in the US (and their families). The ideal candidate should be comfortable with conducting literature reviews, organizing information in excel spreadsheets and drafting and proof-reading written documents. The goals of her lab group are to: 1) conduct exploratory research; 2) build an evidence base for the relationship between housing conditions and older adult health and well-being; 3) identify intervention targets; 4) build relationships with community partners in different sectors; 5) launch Dr. Okoye as a successful independent scientist; 6) develop new scientists to make their mark on the world. Dr. Okoye\u2019s lab group values cooperation and mutual support, work that is engaging and interesting, continual learning and growing, and developing and demonstrating our members\u2019 talents and skills. The Office of Global Health at the Dornsife School of Public Health is dedicated to building a cadre of practitioners and scientists who approach health program planning and scientific questions from a multidisciplinary and entrepreneurial perspective. They place priority on strengthening public health systems and the public health workforce globally and locally. They work closely with ministries of health, NGOs, academic institutions and low- and middle-income country partners to develop mutually beneficial capacity building, training, and research collaborations. OGH pursues this mission by (1) conducting globally-relevant health research to improve health and health equity throughout the world, (2) preparing students to work across cultures to address common global threats, and (3) building the capacity of professionals to address public health challenges through evidence-based programs and policies. This position is grant-funded; employment is contingent upon the continued availability of those funds. Essential Functions Secondary data analysis research support o Support scoping review project Document screening and extraction Set up Covidence templates Be knowledgeable about and support team in applying scoping review best practices o Data analysis Assist with organizing and coding of data from scoping review Assist with organizing and coding of quantitative data from secondary analyses Human subject research support Assist with IRB applications, modifications, and renewals o Assist with creation of recruitment materials and other study materials Assist with screening of potential participants and scheduling of study visits Collect data from study participants, using surveys and semi-structured interviews Assist with organizing and coding of qualitative data General research support o Contribute to manuscripts and grant applications Conduct informal literature reviews and produce summaries to guide project development Draft and edit sections of manuscripts o Generate and edit tables and other data visualizations (e.g., graphs, charts) Conducting literature reviews of papers focused on various aspects of global population shifts Other administrative duties as needed Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master's Degree in MPH, MS, MPA or related field or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 1+ years of experience. Well-organized, competent and excited to contribute to research on older adult health and social determinants of health Expert in reading and writing in English Excellent oral and written communication skills Proficiency in conducting basic statistical analysis and using statistical analysis software (SAS, Stata, R or equivalent) Intermediate or higher level skills in Microsoft Office Suite, and Advanced skill in Excel Attention to detail and accuracy Ability to independently prioritize task completion and to adapt to changes in priorities as needed Preferred Qualifications Experience doing literature reviews Experience with Covidence software Comfort with reading scientific publications Proficiency in quantitative data analysis Proficiency in qualitative methods, data collection and analysis \u2013 or interest in learning Proficiency in data and information visualization Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Non-Exempt, grade F . Compensation for this grade ranges from $15 to $23.31 per hour. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . This is a Full-Time Union position classified as Non-Exempt. Benefits and compensation are based on the agreed Collective Bargaining Agreement for this position. Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) bc32ddfa Last Name (required) 9ecb549d Email (required) bb3ef493 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f67bbf1e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Nursing and Health Professions College of Nursing and Health Professions Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) d935810d Last Name (required) dc2ef015 Email (required) 3d13adc7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/director-finance-operations-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Director, Finance & Operations - University City", "description": "Director, Finance & Operations - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Director, Finance & Operations - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Director, Finance & Operations 507423 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions Full-Time Closing on: Nov 14 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Director of Finance and Operations performs a variety of functions related to business operations, including, but not limited to, budget management, financial and administrative duties including personnel matters for designated divisions within the College of Nursing and Health Professions. This position is responsible for developing and managing procedures needed to ensure appropriate compliance, fiscal controls, budget management and overall fiscal accountability. This position is also responsible for the College\u2019s academic programs data analysis and will work closely with senior leadership in the College to support both short and long-term strategic decision making. Essential Functions Finance Analyzes the Responsibility Centered Management (RCM) budgeting model and develops strategies and make recommendations for the College in regard to program growth, resource allocation, efficiencies, and overall financial success within the RCM model Develops budget projections, including 5-year models, using enrollment and other program data Provides academic programs with detailed analyses on program growth and revenue generation to be used in the decision-making process when allocating resources Manages projects as requested by College Leadership, including environmental scans to identify best practices for financial management including RCM, indirect recovery, RBO and other models using both internal and external sources Manages and tracks all financial transactions; preparation of annual budget reports, business activity reports and financial position forecasts Tracks and reconciles account revenue & expenses for all College funds Analyzes financial details of past, present and expected operations to identify areas where improvements are needed Prepares financial reports for College leadership and University administrators as well as external agencies, i.e. accrediting bodies Provides training and assistance to CNHP staff on Drexel systems, such as the EPAF system, Payment Net, Smart Source, and Page Up Responsible for tracking completion rates and effectively communicating with all faculty and professional staff for the Annual Enterprise Learning requirements to ensure 100% compliance across the college Posts open positions for adjunct, staff and faculty positions in the applicant tracking system - Act as the custodian for the asset management approval process Administration Serves as an advisor to Dean and College leadership & assists in facilitating effective decision making Regularly collaborates with HR Business Partner to develop strategies related to workforce planning, retention plans and ensure compliance with HR policies and procedures Oversees the hiring process for all College hires including the drafting of faculty contracts Assist chairs and administrators with problems involving personnel matters and payroll issues Provides reporting for new hires and terminations to College administrators Acts as a liaison to Human Resources, HRIS, Payroll, Procurement and other University offices Reviews, revises and maintains job descriptions for staff members and faculty serving in administrative roles Maintains departmental and personnel files Data Analysis Provide leadership with data needed to make strategic decisions with regard to enrollment, research, pedagogy, and recruitment by performing qualitative and quantitative data analysis. Gather and analyze college level data to submit to external sources (accreditations, US News, etc.) Assist in reviewing accreditation standards and providing data and feedback for self-study reviews and support developing assessment measures for accreditation reports. Support the development of appropriate processes, structures, tools, and resources for the college to execute strategic priorities by presenting recommendations, alternatives, and implications based on data analysis. Facilities Assist with facilities operations at CNHP locations in the Health Sciences Building and the Academic Building Assist with contracted services and vendors supporting CNHP facilities Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 7+ years of experience Minimum of seven years\u2019 experience in finance and/or accounting and experience in higher education Possess excellent oral, written, analytical and interpersonal skills Ability to outline and present financial models and analyses for various audiences Excellent computer skills including the ability to master software applications related to the role Possess subject matter expertise including knowledge of Web Finance, Web Salary and other Drexel University financial management tools Preferred Qualifications MBA preferred Ability to work collaboratively with leadership, faculty, and staff Ability to work independently and with initiative in planning and implementing Possess strong customer service focus Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade N . Compensation for this grade ranges from $99,720.00 to $149,580.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 578c0a0b Last Name (required) 1b47b02d Email (required) de0f726a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 139aa7d4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Nursing and Health Professions College of Nursing and Health Professions Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) b18895e9 Last Name (required) 556c5ee6 Email (required) 1674f081 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/senior-technical-services-specialist-full-time-salus-campus-elkins-park-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Senior Technical Services Specialist - Full Time - Salus Campus", "description": "Senior Technical Services Specialist - Full Time - Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Senior Technical Services Specialist - Full Time - Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Senior Technical Services Specialist - Full Time 507412 Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania Pennsylvania College of Optometry Full-Time Closing on: Nov 13 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Senior Technical Services Specialist provides technical and administrative support to the Ophthalmic Repair Department and the Department of Technology Services. This includes the installation, maintenance, operation, repair, and transportation of related equipment. The specialist also performs all functions related to the demonstration, sale, and maintenance of student medical equipment. Essential Functions Maintain and repair Optometric equipment Tracking student equipment orders and coordinating with vendors for pricing, receiving, and distribution. Working with the Associate Director, Clinical Systems and the Finance department tracking student orders, and sales. Mentoring repair technicians and assisting the Associate Director, Clinical Systems with ordering parts, tools, and materials, including inventory control. Designing, engineering, and fabricating optical equipment, instruments, aids, and accessories. Coordinating the loaner instrument program and assisting in the sale and disposal of obsolete equipment. Drive & operate Drexel University\u2019s Mobile Unit for Health Resources (MUHR) and other vehicles in a safe, reliable and efficient manner to meet the needs of the University\u2019s community-based clinical activities. Aid while on site at the community-based activities. Collaborate with faculty to confirm required equipment. Order equipment for students in the OD & PA programs. Coordinate equipment distribution to students. Respond to student inquiries about their equipment. Manage equipment warranties, which involves contacting manufacturers and sending back broken or repairable items. Design, engineer, and fabricate optical equipment, instruments, low vision aids, teaching aids, research/development equipment, and computer accessories as needed. Repair, adjust, and clean optics. Calibrate, troubleshoot, and mechanically and electrically repair a wide variety of ophthalmic instruments, including both modern and obsolete models, such as keratometers, refractors, biomicroscopes, lensometers, acuity projectors, perimeters, radiuscopes, examination chairs and stands, indirect ophthalmoscopes, and microscopes. Maintain and operate all ophthalmic and audiovisual equipment at the University and satellite sites. Assist with supporting the University's automated ophthalmic equipment at EP, TEI, and remote Salus satellite clinics. Assist with supporting audiovisual equipment in lab and classroom environments as required. Assist with the installation, configuration, troubleshooting, and repair of biomedical equipment, including M&S charts and other exam room and lab-specific equipment. Supervise and mentor ophthalmic technicians and students on machinery techniques, instrument maintenance procedures, room layouts, mirror system layouts, and low vision lens drilling. Work with the Associate Director, Clinical Systems to contact vendors for pricing and availability of parts, bulbs, metals, woods, plastics, tools, and machine tools, and place orders. Solicit vendors for low bids on new ophthalmic equipment. Dispose of obsolete equipment. Coordinate the loaner instrument program with Salus and instrument manufacturer's representatives and distribute equipment as necessary. Work with the Associate Director, Clinical Systems to control the inventory of stock parts and instrument bulbs in the repair section, as well as stock of metals, plastic, nuts, bolts, and other supplies in the instrument shop. Manage inventory of equipment and its movement between satellite sites and the main campus and maintain inventory control for the business office. Work with the Associate Director, Clinical Systems to manage Procurement Orders on behalf of the responsible Cost Center for parts, bulbs, instrument covers, and materials used for equipment repair and project fabrication. Operate University vehicles safely, legally and efficiently, transporting University staff and students to and from destinations and related activities, . Conduct comprehensive pre and post travel inspections to ensure safe operating conditions and cleanliness of mobile unit/vehicle. Document all mechanical malfunctions and equipment damage on pre and post trip log and turn into facilities to be addressed. Verify the trip itinerary at the time of loading to ensure all parties are aware of details and times. Oversee and assist in the loading and unloading of passengers and equipment set up, as well as the safe storage and securement of equipment and supplies. Allow only authorized passengers in the vehicle and reports unauthorized passengers to the Associated Director and to the screening team leader (Doctor providing care). Maintain all supply levels on the Mobile Unit for Health Resources (MUHR) unit. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Vocational or Technical School in or High School Diploma Experience in design, engineering, and fabrication of optical and related equipment and instruments. Basic computer troubleshooting skills Experience negotiating the purchase of equipment, materials, and supplies. Experience in inventory control. Familiarity with OSHA safety rules and regulations. Ability to represent the college professionally. Ability to lift and move large pieces of equipment safely. Maintain any and all appropriate state driver's licenses Minimum of 5 years of commercial, fire apparatus or Motor Home driving experience of at least 30\u2019 or longer. No driving license suspensions in the past ten years. Ability to read and interpret GPS, maps, and other navigational systems. Available to work evenings and weekends CDL or CDL Recreation license for at least 5 years Light maintenance in Automotive, electrical and/or mechanical Valid driver\u2019s license in state of residence with an acceptable driving record Physical Demands Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 50lbs Location Salus Campus - Elkins Park Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade I. Compensation for this grade ranges from $21.71 to $32.57 per hour. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. Additional Required Documents A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) cdcf6f3b Last Name (required) d2eaf7de Email (required) 714e77a1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 81ed4114 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Pennsylvania College of Optometry Pennsylvania College of Optometry Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 5cdaca34 Last Name (required) 861f609b Email (required) 234ebbc7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/fire-and-emergency-services-specialist-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Fire and Emergency Services Specialist - University City", "description": "Fire and Emergency Services Specialist - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Fire and Emergency Services Specialist - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Fire and Emergency Services Specialist 507393 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Drexel University Finance and Administration Part-Time Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Fire and Emergency Services Specialist (FES Specialist) is responsible for anticipating, recognizing, evaluating, and controlling fire and safety hazards in leased and Drexel-owned facilities. Under direction, you will work closely with Drexel departments to minimize fire and safety risks and manage compliance with applicable University policies and fire code requirements. The FES Specialist will also apply the five tenets of emergency management (prevention, mitigation, preparedness, response, and recovery) to fulfill the mission of the Department of Public Safety. Essential Functions Assist with comprehensive safety and fire code audits of university departments and buildings and submit work orders via the work order management system. Work with internal/external departments to correct fire safety hazards and develop preventive procedures. Assist with delivering training classes and outreach materials. Serve as a system administrator for the Drexel Business Continuity Platform. In the absence of the Director or Assistant Director, act as a representative to other departments, which includes acting as a technical advisor on fire safety and emergency preparedness issues. Write reports documenting observations and recommendations for Director\u2019s review. Assist with writing reports to other departments. Document all work in office computer files and databases. Assist in coordinating and managing the Building Emergency Response Team (BERT) operations and safety protocols. Contribute to Drexel\u2019s overall Emergency Operations Planning. Be available to work flexible hours (nights and weekends). Under supervision of the Assistant Director or the Director, performs assigned tasks using standard procedures. Expected to act with increasing independence but all work will be reviewed by an Assistant Director or Director. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a HS Diploma or GED. Minimum of 2-3 years of code enforcement, fire service, facility auditing, emergency preparedness, or relevant experience. Valid driver\u2019s license from the state of residence. Preferred Qualifications Higher education degree in Fire Science, Safety, Public Safety Administration, Emergency Management or related field. Fire Inspector I or Commercial Building Inspector, CPR, ICS/NIMS. Fire Protection Specialist, Fire Inspector II, PA or NREMT. Knowledge of local, state, and national fire codes and regulations pertaining to fire safety and fire code compliance. Knowledge of the principles of emergency management/disaster response and recovery. Knowledge of organizational and personnel management skills. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to work within a team setting. Ability to use computer databases and spreadsheet programs. Ability to locate and use appropriate technical resources in fire safety. Ability to lift and carry materials and equipment. Physically able to serve on response team. Developed professional presentation skills. Possesses knowledge of basic theories, concepts, practices, and procedures in fire safety and emergency management. Applies the knowledge to work assignments to meet specific department goals and objectives. Develops solutions to problems of limited scope. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 50lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This is a Part-Time per diem position classified as Non-Exempt. The offered pay is based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Per Diem/Casual/Temporary Benefit Fact Sheet . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 582502cc Last Name (required) 1950ed43 Email (required) 38848f2d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 25dd3b37 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Finance and Administration Drexel University Finance and Administration Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) aaed3a6f Last Name (required) 104176bf Email (required) bcb9ce23 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/operations-data-analyst-hybrid-flexible-work-arrangement-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Operations & Data Analyst", "description": "Operations & Data Analyst - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Operations & Data Analyst - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Operations & Data Analyst 507387 Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University Office of the Provost Full-Time Closing on: Nov 5 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Under the general direction of the Assistant Director for Operations, the Operations and Data Analyst is responsible for maintaining the accuracy and integrity of student records including TPAR setting and changes, student record audits for round reporting. This position is also responsible for the maintenance of the co-op calendar and University Calendar operations. In addition, the position compiles data for annual reports, fact sheets, and various data requests for internal and external constituents. Essential Functions Audit and generate reports for cycle and round data for jobs, applications, interviews and placements. This includes being responsible for notifying Co-op Team Leads and co-op advisors of irregularities and issues that may need follow-up. Monitor student co-op records via the SCDCOps RN queue. Sending and receiving changes via SCDC TPAR mailbox, updating co-op cycles, and collaborate with Steinbright staff to resolve student record issues. Manage daily BannerJob Output data. Receiving job output and monitoring the students records via SCDC Ops mailbox, updating co-op cycles, and collaborate with Steinbright staff to resolve student record issues. Serve as support contact and direct concerns to the appropriate department for Steinbright systems and database functions in Banner, DrexelOne, OAS, TimeTrade, etc. Process ad-hoc data requests from external Drexel departments and Steinbright employer partners. Prepare, review, and audit reports and manage communications for the department. Assist with assessing and analyzing Steinbright processes and procedures. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information). Minimum of 2 years relevant professional work experience. High level proficiency with MS Office. Intermediate to advance level Excel experience. Proven ability to learn and adapt to new technical skills. Ability to generate and analyze reports from database systems. Ability to accurately track details and handle multiple assignments simultaneously in fast-paced environment. Ability to interact effectively with multiple departments within the university. Proven ability to take initiative and work both independently and in a team. Ability to exercise discretion and judgment with sensitive and confidential matters. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Banner and OAS or similar systems preferred. Location Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade J. Compensation for this grade ranges from $ 52,360.00 to $ 78,530.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. #LI-Hybrid Apply Now First Name (required) b6faa93e Last Name (required) 050bab91 Email (required) 0afaa438 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a6eeea9d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Office of the Provost Drexel University Office of the Provost Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) cbe83c7f Last Name (required) f08d5088 Email (required) 5b4abf57 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/department-administrator-english-philosophy-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Department Administrator, English & Philosophy - University City", "description": "Department Administrator, English & Philosophy - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Department Administrator, English & Philosophy - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Department Administrator, English & Philosophy 507340 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Arts & Sciences Drexel University Full-Time Closing on: Oct 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary College of Arts and Sciences (CoAS), Department of English & Philosophy, is seeking an organized, analytical, courteous, and proactive Department Administrator who is skilled in managing multiple tasks independently while delivering superior customer service to join our team of faculty and staff. Under the direction of the Department Head, the successful candidate will be responsible for planning and administering the academic, operational, and financial activities within the Department and will be committed to providing attentive support to all faculty, staff, and students, ensuring consistent, efficient operations. The Department Administrator will manage all day-to-day purchasing, hiring, and business processes of the ongoing teaching, research, and scholarship activities within the Department while maintaining compliance with relevant College, university, and government policies. This key role will liaise directly with the Dean\u2019s Office and will help analyze office processes and policies, develop creative solutions to problems, answer operational questions, and take part in decision-making that supports increased efficiencies for the Department and College. Essential Functions Financial Tasks: Ensure that all relevant departmental cost-centers (i.e., unrestricted, restricted, designated, gift), personnel and operating expenses are appropriate, in compliance, and within budget Support departmental leadership on departmental spending, financial objectives, and compliance Oversee all purchasing for the department as well as monthly reconciliation of purchasing card statements Independently manage and document all financial transactions. Complete labor redistributions, journal entries, and other expenses-related tasks as needed. Provide guidance and support to departmental employees on best practices for purchasing, reimbursement and awards/prize distribution, when relevant Prepare annual budget reports, business activity reports, and expense tracking reports Serve as primary budget/administrative contact for the Office of the Dean (CoAS) Under the supervision of the Department Head, liaise with various offices (e.g., Procurement, Office of General Counsel, Human Resources, Comptroller\u2019s Office, Tax Office, Payroll Office, Work Study Office, Drexel Central, Scheduling Team, Graduate Support Team, ISSS, Facilities, Institutional Advancement, University programs and schools, College Grant Administrators, etc.) Personnel Tasks: Process all departmental hiring paperwork for adjuncts, faculty, staff, students, temporary employees, visitors/guests (including tuition remission and summer salary, if relevant) Support the recruitment and onboarding processes for all employees associated with the department Ensure compliance with all Human Resources hiring policies Certify personnel labor is charged to the appropriate funding source Approve time sheets for employees, if/as needed (e.g. monthly employees and biweekly employees, etc.) Establish an active network of professional contacts to support the execution of departmental business operations Help create and maintain a database of all departmental contracts and track faculty teaching loads in collaboration with CoAS Supervise support staff within the department; conduct staff meetings, if relevant Administrative Tasks: Execute all day-to-day business processes, developing and implementing procedures in compliance with university policy, federal regulations, and contractual requirements Manage and/or provide oversight of departmental space, where pertinent, which includes but is not limited to stocking departmental space with business and academic supplies, submitting work orders, overseeing phone lines and office equipment, and attending to space requests Oversee and support routine departmental events which includes but is not limited to advertising, reserving space, arranging meetings, booking travel, and ordering food Maintain departmental physical and digital records in compliance with the University\u2019s record retention policy Support faculty life-cycle processes, including the Promotion & Tenure Process of tenure track and teaching faculty Assist with reports, if necessary Provide direction and advice to all employees, students, and vendors with business and academic operational questions Resolve problems with the highest level of customer service Oversee select department-specific academic processes such as curriculum updates in Courseleaf and language placement exams Liaise and coordinate with the College scheduling team so that the team can ensure proper instructional assignments, course offerings, classroom spaces, etc. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 5 years of experience directly related to higher education, budget management, and/or customer service. Strong interpersonal skills and collegiality. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Excellent computer skills including proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (high proficiency with Excel). Exceptional analytical skills and ability to oversee highly confidential information. Strong communication skills both written and verbal. Strong customer services skills. Excellent attention to detail and multi-tasking skills. Demonstrated commitment to follow-through of assigned tasks and projects. Ability to utilize critical thinking skills and judgment in problem-solving and decision-making, or escalating issues as needed. Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade K. Compensation for this grade ranges from $60,240 - $90,350 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 90ba3f7b Last Name (required) 4e00a366 Email (required) f49e16aa Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 95639ba1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences Drexel University College of Arts & Sciences Drexel University Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 44a93dba Last Name (required) 95df8e4e Email (required) 7ffd5b1a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/shop-monitor-evenings-and-weekends-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Shop Monitor (Evenings and Weekends) - University City", "description": "Shop Monitor (Evenings and Weekends) - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Shop Monitor (Evenings and Weekends) - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Shop Monitor (Evenings and Weekends) 507326 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Drexel University Westphal College of Media Arts & Design Part-Time Closing on: Oct 23 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Assist Fabrication Facilities Manager, Students and Faculty by overseeing the safe and effective operation of the equipment and maintenance of the Design Arts Annex lab on a day-to-day basis. Essential Functions Oversee the safe and effective operation of the Design Arts Annex shop facility. Implement and enforce shop standards/policies and safety rules. Provide introductory support to students regarding course projects. Assist students with technical advice/assistance on process and procedures. Ensure that students are operating toots & machinery safely and correctly Provide occasional providence of shop training/orientation sessions and working guidelines for Interior or Architecture students that will be qualified to use the facilities and equipment. Supervise and conduct maintenance and repair of shop tools, equipment, and the shop environment. Maintain standards of cleanliness in the shop. Other tasks assigned by Fabrication Facilities Manager. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree. Minimum of 2 years of experience with woodworking equipment and tools, and 1 year of experience with welding (MIG), metal working tools and equipment. Ability to work evenings and weekends. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 50lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This is a Part-Time casual position classified as Non-Exempt. The offered pay is based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Per Diem/Casual/Temporary Benefit Fact Sheet . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 6b5e2b80 Last Name (required) 0c30bc24 Email (required) b3a01aa2 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 34e304c6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Westphal College of Media Arts & Design Drexel University Westphal College of Media Arts & Design Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) bea7100c Last Name (required) 0b948987 Email (required) 4bc73800 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-recruitment-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Director of Recruitment - University City", "description": "Assistant Director of Recruitment - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Assistant Director of Recruitment - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Assistant Director of Recruitment 507327 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Drexel University Westphal College of Media Arts & Design Full-Time Closing on: Nov 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Responsible for recruiting qualified undergraduate and graduate applicants for admission into the Antoinette Westphal College of Media Arts & Design, the Assistant Director of Recruitment plans strategically how to improve conversion rates for each aspect of the admissions funnel; records, updates, and analyzes recruiting data; contributes to marketing and yield campaigns that help to attract and yield prospective students; makes ROI assessments of recruitment marketing campaigns. As a key member of the Recruitment team, the Assistant Director coordinates and participates in on- and off-campus recruiting activities such as presentations, college fairs, o\ufb03ce and campus interviews, conferences, and other platforms as needed. Works to enhance school brand and reputation while being the main recruiter on the road for Westphal. The Assistant Director also analyzes and develops potential markets for undergraduate, graduate, and transfer populations. Working with faculty and College leadership, the Assistant Director develops a keen understanding of the various undergraduate and graduate programs, and other educational offerings in Westphal College in order to effectively match opportunities to prospective students. Essential Functions Participate in appropriate recruitment and enrollment activities including open houses, regional presentations, National Portfolio Day events, receptions, admitted student\u2019s day events, college fairs, information sessions, conferences, and more. Travel on behalf of the College for recruitment and other college-related events. Present to individuals and groups both on and off campus to educate them about the Westphal College of Media Arts & Design and its academic programs. Spend a portion of time supporting Graduate recruitment and enrollment strategies. Manage and respond to prospective student phone e-mail and web inquiries received by Westphal College. Assist in the development and maintenance of the Westphal College\u2019s recruitment and marketing plan with the purpose of promoting the College\u2019s visibility and general recruitment efforts. Develop and monitor statistical reports to enhance recruitment strategies, yield management, forecasting, and operational efficiency. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's or Master's Degree in an art, design or media discipline, or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 1 year of college admissions or student recruitment experience. Ability to review portfolios in art, design or media disciplines. Ability to effectively communicate in person and in writing and speak publicly. High energy, attention to detail, and the ability to organize effectively. Valid Driver\u2019s License with ability to travel domestically and internationally a few times a year. Ability to work evenings and weekends as necessary. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with various student populations in a student enrollment, recruitment, or admissions capacity. Experience with production of a variety of media, particularly print publications. Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade J. Compensation for this grade ranges from $52,360 - $78,530 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 5e87f95e Last Name (required) eb2b4692 Email (required) aeb5061d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 68b1a474 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Westphal College of Media Arts & Design Drexel University Westphal College of Media Arts & Design Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) f5d1f1d3 Last Name (required) f754a627 Email (required) 7a1fb142 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/senior-community-health-worker-peer-community-outreach-team-center-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Senior Community Health Worker Peer, Community Outreach Team - Center City", "description": "Senior Community Health Worker Peer, Community Outreach Team - Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Senior Community Health Worker Peer, Community Outreach Team - Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Senior Community Health Worker Peer, Community Outreach Team 507372 Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Dornsife School of Public Health Full-Time Closing on: Nov 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary We are seeking a compassionate and experienced individual to fill the role of Senior Community Health Worker Practitioner (CHWP) at both the Community Outreach Team (COT) and Youth Advisory Board (YAB) programs, affiliated with the Center for Nonviolence and Social Justice at Drexel University's Dornsife School of Public Health. The successful candidate will split their time between providing support to the Youth Advisory Board, partnering with community organizations, and remote work, ensuring the delivery of comprehensive community health services. This position is grant-funded; employment is contingent upon the continued availability of those funds. Essential Functions Outreach and Engagement: Conduct in-person outreach and engagement activities at various partner sites, including YouthBuild, Students Run Philly Style, and other youth-focused organizations. Develop trusting relationships with potential clients based on lived experience. Assist in identifying and participating in at least 1 resource fair and other tabling event per month. Program Development: Assist in the development and implementation of interventions at partner sites, including the CYPHER (Community of Young People Healing, Experiencing, and Rebuilding) groups, which are culturally relevant trauma recovery groups. Supervision and Mentorship: Provide guidance and mentorship to COT's CHWPs and to CNSJ interns. Act as a key contact for staff at partner sites and contribute to the development of site-specific interventions. Documentation and Reporting: Maintain accurate records of patient interactions, program activities, and outcomes. Ensure compliance with funding requirements and organizational guidelines. Training and Onboarding: Facilitate training activities for new CHWPs and interns, including shadowing, orientation, and evaluation of internship experiences. Youth Advisory Board Coordination: Facilitate recruitment, onboarding, and retention of YAB members; planning and facilitating bi-weekly meetings, workshops, and events; supporting youth leadership and skill development; providing mentorship and ongoing support to YAB members; and serving as a liaison between youth members and organizational leadership to ensure youth voices are incorporated into programs, policies, and decision-making. Required Qualifications Minimum of a HS Diploma or GED Minimum of 4 years of experience. Pennsylvania Peer Specialist and Community Health Worker Peer (CHWP) Certification required Minimum of 4 years\u2019 experience providing peer services to violently injured people Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Location Center City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade I. Compensation for this grade ranges from $45,330 to $68,000 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 38998d22 Last Name (required) df9eb566 Email (required) dbc1019a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert aab4ccd6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Dornsife School of Public Health Dornsife School of Public Health Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 069a5959 Last Name (required) d8f17b49 Email (required) af7bea05 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/adjunct-community-health-prevention-chp-remote-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Adjunct, Community Health & Prevention (CHP)", "description": "Adjunct, Community Health & Prevention (CHP) - Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Adjunct, Community Health & Prevention (CHP) - Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Adjunct, Community Health & Prevention (CHP) 507368 Remote, Pennsylvania Dornsife School of Public Health Part-Time Closing on: Oct 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites About Drexel Drexel University fulfills its founder's vision of preparing each new generation of students for productive professional and civic lives while also focusing the University's collective expertise on solving society's greatest problems. Drexel is an academically comprehensive and globally engaged urban research university, dedicated to advancing knowledge and society and to providing every student with a valuable, rigorous, experiential, technology-infused education, enriched by the nation's premier cooperative education program. The Dana and David Dornsife School of Public Health was founded on the principle of health as a human right and the recognition of the importance of social justice as a means to achieve health for all. The Graduate School of Public Health is ranked 19th in the nation by U.S. News & World Report, and we are proud to be ranked first in the City of Philadelphia. As part of a top-tier comprehensive research university, students benefit from specialized research centers and cross-disciplinary collaborations within the University, the City of Philadelphia and throughout the world. Job Summary Multiple courses may be available for Academic Year 2026-2027 in the Department of Community Health & Prevention including courses in behavior and social change theories, community theory and health practice, health communication, measuring health outcomes, outcomes and impact evaluation, global health, public health ethics, and history of public health. These courses have been taught previously, so previously used syllabi and course materials are available. The adjunct faculty member will select course materials in accordance with the approved course description, foster active learning in all students, maintain proper course-related records, evaluate student work, and provide students with feedback. Courses that enroll 30 or more will usually have a teaching assistant. Some courses are online and asynchronous, others are in-person on Drexel\u2019s University City campus. The School of Public Health is on the quarter system and each course is ten weeks long, with three hours of instruction per week. The full calendar can be viewed at https://drexel.edu/provost/policies-calendars/academic-calendars/quarters-2022-2024/ Essential Functions Teach required number of credit hours per quarter Plan and provide instructional experiences that reflect an understanding of the philosophy, objectives, and curriculum of the program Provide instruction consistent with approved course descriptions Evaluate student achievement of curricular objectives/outcomes Maintain communication with the department chair and program director regarding any course or student issues Supervise a teaching assistant, if one is assigned to the course Perform other similar duties as assigned Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in public health, social sciences, medicine, bioethics, history of science, or related areas. Must have teaching experience at the graduate or undergraduate level. If applying for a course focusing on global issues, global expertise is necessary. Special Instructions to the Applicant Applications should consist of a brief cover letter indicating which Drexel courses are of interest and describing your qualifications to teach them, a CV, and a list of references. Letters of reference will be requested from candidates who are invited for an interview. Electronic submissions in PDF format are required. Review of applicants will be ongoing until all adjunct teaching positions are full. Apply Now First Name (required) 41c623f2 Last Name (required) 7551c003 Email (required) 1f541521 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a0ce40d1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Dornsife School of Public Health Dornsife School of Public Health Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations Remote, Pennsylvania, United States Remote, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) b280e399 Last Name (required) af09206b Email (required) 7abd1965 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-research-fellow-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states-8250802e-2afb-47ea-9d39-c1846787ffd4": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow - University City", "description": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Postdoctoral Research Fellow - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Postdoctoral Research Fellow 507297 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Computing and Informatics College of Engineering Drexel University Full-Time Closing on: Oct 22 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Deak Laboratory at Drexel University is seeking a highly motivated individual to join our interdisciplinary research program at the interface of immunology, biomaterials, and chemical engineering. The position is supported by two recently funded NIH R01 projects focused on engineering immune responses for immune tolerance and therapeutic vaccination against HIV. Our laboratory develops biomaterial and chemistry-based approaches to manipulate dendritic cell function and downstream adaptive immune responses. Current projects include engineering tolerogenic dendritic cells for durable, antigen-specific immune tolerance and developing liposomal nanotrap therapeutic vaccines that capture viral particles and redirect them toward productive antigen-presenting cell responses. These projects integrate chemical synthesis, lipid and polymeric biomaterials, nanoparticle formulation and characterization, cellular immunology, flow cytometry, and in vivo studies. We are particularly interested in a scientist who can take a leadership role within the laboratory while remaining actively engaged in experimental research. The successful candidate will work closely with the PI to coordinate these newly funded projects, mentor junior researchers, and help maintain an organized and productive laboratory environment. This position is grant-funded; employment is contingent upon the continued availability of those funds. Essential Functions Lead and coordinate research activities associated with NIH-funded projects in immune tolerance engineering and therapeutic vaccination. Design, conduct, analyze, and interpret experiments involving biomaterials and immune-cell interactions. Prepare and characterize liposomal, lipid-based, and polymeric biomaterial systems. Perform or oversee chemical synthesis and conjugation of biomaterial components and targeting molecules. Conduct immunological assays, including mammalian cell culture, immune-cell isolation and differentiation, flow cytometry, and related functional assays. Coordinate experiments across students, collaborators, and project personnel and help maintain progress toward project milestones. Mentor graduate and undergraduate students in experimental design, laboratory techniques, data analysis, and scientific communication. Assist with laboratory organization and administration, including ordering, inventory management, equipment maintenance, protocol development, and implementation of laboratory procedures. Contribute to manuscripts, presentations, progress reports, and future grant applications. Promote rigorous experimental practices, clear documentation, and an organized and collaborative laboratory environment Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a PhD or Doctorate in Chemical engineering, biomedical engineering, bioengineering, immunology, chemistry, pharmaceutical sciences, materials science, or a closely related field or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 5-10 years of research experience. Research experience in immunology, bioengineering or immunoengineering. Experience with chemical synthesis, biomaterials, drug delivery, nanoparticles, or lipid-based systems. Strong experimental, analytical, and scientific communication skills. Strong organizational skills and attention to experimental documentation and laboratory operations. Preferred Qualifications Experience with dendritic cells, T-cell immunology, immune tolerance, vaccines, or viral immunology. Experience with liposomes, lipid nanoparticles, polymeric particles, or related drug-delivery systems. Experience with lipid or small-molecule synthesis, bioconjugation, or surface functionalization. Experience with multicolor flow cytometry and primary immune-cell culture. Experience with animal studies and analysis of immune responses in vivo. Previous experience mentoring students or coordinating research projects. Demonstrated leadership and laboratory-management skills. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade K . Compensation for this grade ranges from $60,240.00 - $90,350.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. Applicants should submit a CV, brief statement of research experience and interests (<1 page), and contact information for references. The research statement should highlight relevant experience in immunology, biomaterials, chemical synthesis, and/or research leadership. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) cf2ad866 Last Name (required) 7c34484b Email (required) 7a745a7e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 238a5302 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Computing and Informatics College of Engineering Drexel University College of Computing and Informatics College of Engineering Drexel University Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) ee9739d4 Last Name (required) b7a139d9 Email (required) ae525c0e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/advanced-practice-provider-center-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states-22de4d56-929c-4d93-8e69-a1257f1cdef8": {"title": "Advanced Practice Provider - Center City", "description": "Advanced Practice Provider - Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Advanced Practice Provider - Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Advanced Practice Provider 507375 Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Medicine Full-Time Closing on: Nov 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Advanced Practice Provider (Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant) plays a crucial role within the ambulatory care environment, collaborating closely with a multidisciplinary healthcare team. The Advanced Practice Provider is responsible for delivering comprehensive care within an Internal Medicine practice, focusing on adult patients. Essential Functions Conduct assessments, diagnoses, and management of patients in a primary care setting. Provide preventive health services, including routine visits, screenings, and immunizations, and address acute and complex care needs. Collaborate with an interdisciplinary healthcare team to ensure optimal patient outcomes. Evaluate patient risk factors, encompassing physical, socioeconomic, and psychosocial aspects. Gather and document comprehensive patient histories and perform thorough physical examinations. Order, conduct, and interpret necessary diagnostic tests, responding to results that require further evaluation. Develop differential diagnoses and engage with collaborative physicians as needed. Coordinate care with specialists when necessary. Formulate and document individualized plans of care based on patient needs. Utilize evidence-based guidelines to create dynamic care plans applicable across various patient scenarios. Implement and adjust care plans based on patient responses and diagnostic findings. Prescribe appropriate diagnostic and therapeutic interventions. Perform in-office procedures within the scope of practice. Documentation: All outpatient visits must be documented in the EPIC system using the SOAP format. Ensure timely documentation that meets compliance standards, capturing essential patient information including history, presenting issues, physical exams, diagnoses, and treatment plans. - Additional Responsibilities: Review diagnostic study results promptly and communicate follow-up plans to patients. Address messages and inquiries through the Epic portal. Review specialist consults and inpatient summaries to maintain comprehensive patient records. Provide coverage for in-basket messages as needed. Provide on call coverage as assigned by Medical Director Communication and Collaboration: Maintain ongoing communication with office staff and the interdisciplinary healthcare team, ensuring effective collaboration with patients and their care teams. - Quality and Productivity: Engage with the population health team to enhance patient access and outcomes, striving to meet annual quality metrics as defined by the organization. 10% - Professional Development: Demonstrate professional practice behaviors, including mentoring and educating students. Seek opportunities for involvement in research and evidence-based practice analysis. Maintain national board certification, state licensure, and required continuing education. - Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master's Degree in or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of Minimum of 2 years working experience as an Advanced Care Provider in a clinical care environment. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Location Center City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade N . Compensation for this grade ranges from $99,720.00 to $149,580.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) e68569f9 Last Name (required) cd524ff1 Email (required) 6f06d48d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 6e0a4b73 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Medicine College of Medicine Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) d081d71d Last Name (required) 218369fd Email (required) 862b4309 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-teaching-professor-of-health-sciences-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor of Health Sciences - University City", "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor of Health Sciences - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor of Health Sciences - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor of Health Sciences 507043 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions Drexel University Full-Time Closing on: Nov 11 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Department of Health Sciences at Drexel University invites applications for a non-tenure track faculty position at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor whose whose primary responsibility will be teaching research-related courses to undergraduate students. These courses may include research methods, statistics, and/or a newly developed research seminar centered on the candidate's area of expertise and current research interests. A secondary responsibility will be teaching courses in human anatomy and physiology. Successful candidates will be dedicated to teaching with an inclusive philosophy and enthusiastic about establishing a line of scholarship and service that supports academic career growth and the department\u2019s mission of engaging undergraduate students in a range of experiential learning opportunities. A major focus of the position is helping the department achieve its teaching mission. Protected time for research, service, and career development will be provided as appropriate. Candidates who have expertise in content areas associated with major chronic health conditions are of particular interest for the department; these content areas include, but are not limited to: cardiovascular physiology, muscle physiology, aging, and genetics. Candidates who bring a line of scholarship that can enhance the department\u2019s emerging emphasis on creating an undergraduate research experience for all undergraduates are especially encouraged to apply. About the Department of Health Sciences: This is an exciting time of development within the Department of Health Sciences. In 2022, we moved into a new state-of-the-art building on Drexel\u2019s main campus that also houses the College of Medicine. The Department of Health Sciences administers a large and expanding Bachelor of Science in Health Sciences program for students pursuing careers in a variety of healthcare fields, many requiring graduate education. Common fields of study for undergraduates in the department are physician assistant, physical therapy, and exercise science. In-progress department initiatives include expanding the undergraduate research program, growing our new health-focused exercise science major, and participating in the University\u2019s academic transformation initiatives. Opportunities for collaboration exist within the College of Nursing and Health Professions and with researchers in the College of Medicine, College of Engineering, School of Biomedical Engineering, and School of Public Health. Additional opportunities are offered through the many universities, health care centers, and community partnerships in the Philadelphia region. Essential Functions Teaching research-related courses to undergraduate students. These courses may include research methods, statistics, and/or a newly developed research seminar centered on the candidate's area of expertise and current research interests. Teaching courses in human anatomy and physiology. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a PhD or comparable doctoral degree Minimum of 1+ years of experience teaching in higher education Experience with development of multimedia and integration of technology in an academic setting Strong communication and inter-personal skills Commitment to collaborating with instructors across a shared course and department Commitment to teaching, scholarship, service and growth as an academic faculty member Alignment with the goals and direction of the Health Sciences Department Preferred Qualifications Expertise that compliments our current faculty and potential collaborators within the College of Nursing & Health Professions and Drexel University A defined scholarly agenda related to health sciences Experience with mentoring students in undergraduate research Experience teaching in a gross anatomy lab Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This is a Full-Time Faculty position classified as Exempt. The offered salary is based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Full-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet. Special Instructions to the Applicant Applications should include: 1) a cover letter that outlines the candidate\u2019s qualifications, experience, and interest for the position, 2) a curriculum vitae, 3) a brief statement of teaching philosophy and interests, 4) a brief statement of the candidate\u2019s research/scholarship agenda and goals, and 5) names of three references that can be contacted if the applicant is selected. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 17ea95a1 Last Name (required) b5695fd4 Email (required) e2a8b9c9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 52a70da7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Nursing and Health Professions Drexel University College of Nursing and Health Professions Drexel University Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 530ed222 Last Name (required) a9aa8430 Email (required) b69e0818 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/administrative-assistant-center-for-autism-and-neurodiversity-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Administrative Assistant, Center for Autism and Neurodiversity - University City", "description": "Administrative Assistant, Center for Autism and Neurodiversity - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Administrative Assistant, Center for Autism and Neurodiversity - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Administrative Assistant, Center for Autism and Neurodiversity 507307 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Drexel University Enrollment Management and Student Success Full-Time Closing on: Nov 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Administrative Assistant, Center for Autism and Neurodiversity, will provide administrative and clerical support for the CAN program. This position will also assist with the tasks related to funding received by the Office of Vocational Rehabilitation (OVR). The Administrative Assistant is often the first staff member prospective students, and their families encounter and contribute to creating a welcoming, responsive, and professional experience for all visitors and program participants. The Administrative Assistant is responsible for managing administrative processes, maintaining records, coordinating events and meetings, preparing reports, reconciling expenses, and supporting the daily operations of the department. The successful candidate will be highly organized, detail-oriented, customer-service focused, and capable of managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Essential Functions Manage all correspondence related to prospective students and families. Maintain accurate records of student\u2019s status with the Office of Vocational Rehabilitation (OVR) and communicate regularly with OVR. Act as liaison between CAN, OVR, and Drexel\u2019s Financial Aid office to ensure students\u2019 accounts are accurate and up to date. Create twice-quarterly, quarterly and annual reports for OVR. Establish and maintain files, logs, and other tracking systems for a variety of information, projects, and events; may update website or use social media. Reconcile expenses for the Office. Organize and maintain schedules and make arrangements/preparations as needed, including preparing or providing agendas, meeting minutes, equipment, location, information packets, travel, and follow up action items. Perform clerical tasks such as answering and directing phone calls and ordering office supplies. Submit work orders to the Facilities Department as needed. Plan and convene on and off-campus activities such as the Autism at Work: University Series events, Faculty and Staff Education Series events and working employee breakfasts with the Steinbright Career Development Center (SCDC). This includes reserving space, making all related arrangements for speakers, arranging catering, etc. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a HS Diploma or GED and 5 years of administrative experience. Proficiency with various computer software applications, including Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook). Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain confidentiality. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with various departments. Strong organization and attention to detail skills. Ability to work independently/autonomously under limited supervision. Cultural awareness and competency demonstrated by working with and/or understanding of individuals of diverse identities, including those with different levels of academic preparation, and varying abilities. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communications skills. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's Degree. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 25lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Non-Exempt, grade I. Compensation for this grade ranges from $21.71 - $32.57 per hour. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 7a0ca885 Last Name (required) d9ae9f0b Email (required) 65ab60c5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e6f7dad0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Enrollment Management and Student Success Drexel University Enrollment Management and Student Success Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 02333e6a Last Name (required) 725ece1e Email (required) 28902274 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/part-time-research-assistant-i-queen-lane-campus-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Part-Time Research Assistant I - Queen Lane Campus", "description": "Part-Time Research Assistant I - Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Part-Time Research Assistant I - Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Part-Time Research Assistant I 507376 Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Medicine Part-Time Closing on: Nov 1 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary We are seeking a self-motivated, diligent, and well-organized candidate with a MS or PhD degree in Immunology or related discipline to join our dynamic research team to investigate dendritic cell biology and immunotherapeutic potential against human chronic viral infections and neuroinflammatory diseases. Applicants should have a strong background and advanced technical skills in cell biology, molecular biology and immunology with a keen interest in learning and applying new skills to advance ongoing programs. This position is grant-funded; employment is contingent upon the continued availability of those funds. Essential Functions Competency and proficiency in mammalian cell culture and immune assays, Protein biochemistry and/or, Molecular Biology. Understanding and experience in the area of inflammation would be a plus. Working knowledge and experience in maintaining day-to-day laboratory operation and upkeep. Handle reagent orders and maintain records routinely. Outstanding personal initiative and communication skills (oral and written English). Assisting lab personnel and the PI writing papers and/or scientific projects. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master's Degree in Immunology or related or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 1 year of experience. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Location Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Non-Exempt, grade F . Compensation for this grade ranges from $15 to $23.31 per hour. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) a0ac0d21 Last Name (required) 8b33ca6a Email (required) 77662fb5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 709a254a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Medicine College of Medicine Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 82a09de9 Last Name (required) 6f179a91 Email (required) 24571b41 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/administrative-coordinator-departments-of-chemistry-and-physics-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Administrative Coordinator - Departments of Chemistry and Physics - University City", "description": "Administrative Coordinator - Departments of Chemistry and Physics - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Administrative Coordinator - Departments of Chemistry and Physics - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Administrative Coordinator - Departments of Chemistry and Physics 507360 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Arts & Sciences Drexel University Full-Time Closing on: Nov 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Departments of Chemistry and Physics in the College of Arts and Sciences are seeking an individual with strong administrative and personnel skills to assist in the administrative management of our academic Departments. The Administrative Coordinator works with the Departmental Administrators and Department Heads of the Departments of Chemistry and Physics. Day-to-day duties will be divided between the two departments. Under the direction of and in collaboration with the Department Administrator(s) and Department Heads, oversight and evaluation of this position will be the responsibility of the Chemistry & Physics Department Heads. The Administrative Coordinator should have exceptional communication and problem-solving skills handling office duties and optimizing office operations. We seek an experienced and professional individual who is highly organized, can work independently, is a good problem solver, and has strong verbal and written communication skills. This is an in-person position working on-campus. Essential Functions Manage the physical office space and daily physical operations of the Department(s), including mail sorting and distribution, shipping and receiving packages, managing offices keys and/or space access; processing work orders; managing telecommunications needs; ordering supplies; resolving issues with office equipment; ensuring space is cleaned and trash is picked up regularly; acting as a liaison with Facilities and Environmental Health & Safety Act as first point of contract for departmental guests, greeting and directing visitors with a pleasant and collegial attitude Manage and coordinate the departmental calendars and oversee any departmental schedules such as faculty office hours, student help sessions, and departmental meetings and events Manage the departmental general email inboxes and provide support for any departmental listservs Support the management of physical and digital files; maintain compliance with university record retention policies Answer and direct telephone calls Manage ordering and scheduled deliveries for select external Chemistry and Physics vendors; Communicate with account representatives on pricing, backorders, delivery issues and tax-exempt status requirements Provide logistical support for departmental events in coordination with other departmental staff Organize travel arrangements for faculty and departmental guests Ensure faculty books orders are submitted Collect and organize syllabi for all courses offered by the Departments Compose, type, and distribute meeting notes, routine correspondence, and reports Perform general administrative, clerical, and executive support tasks Provide support to departmental faculty and committees, staff, students, and guests Assist in miscellaneous duties as requested by the Department Administrators and/or Department Head in Chemistry or Physics Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a HS Diploma or GED and 3 years of administrative experience. Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communications skills. Excellent customer service skills. Proficient with MS Office Suite including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Ability to switch gears depending on processing and/or project deadlines, and remain flexible/adapt to changing priorities. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Ability to work occasional evenings to support events. Preferred Qualifications Associate's degree Familiarity with higher education in the sciences Experience with Banner Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 25lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Non-Exempt, grade H . Compensation for this grade ranges from $18.89 - $28.33 per hour. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 229ac2c8 Last Name (required) 4059bb66 Email (required) e8f0f847 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e43f644b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences Drexel University College of Arts & Sciences Drexel University Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) c0c54a25 Last Name (required) 5c309ef8 Email (required) 44854baa Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/assistant-director-donor-relations-hybrid-flexible-work-arrangement-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Director, Donor Relations", "description": "Assistant Director, Donor Relations - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Assistant Director, Donor Relations - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Assistant Director, Donor Relations 507255 Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University Institutional Advancement Full-Time Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Assistant Director, Donor Relations is an important member of the stewardship team within the Office of Institutional Advancement (IA). This position is responsible for managing donor acknowledgements for all gifts to the University, including those on behalf of Schools and Colleges, the Senior Vice President of IA and the University President. Additionally, this role supports a portfolio of tailored stewardship writing needs across IA, including tribute letters, event remarks, ad hoc Presidential letters, and other special projects. The Assistant Director, Donor Relations partners closely with donor relations and development communications teammates, engagement peers, annual giving, frontline fundraisers, the Office of the President, and other key stakeholders to ensure cohesive, high-quality, and timely donor communications. This is a hybrid position, working in-person 1-2 days a week as needed. Essential Functions Write and/or manage acknowledgements for gifts of all sizes on a weekly basis. Duties include pulling and organizing data, updating language on automated acknowledgement emails, adjusting templated letters for Major Gifts donors, and writing bespoke language for Principal-level gifts. Write, review, and oversee the signing and mailing of ad hoc Presidential letters to alumni, donors, and friends. Write and send tribute letters for gifts in honor and in memorial, on a biweekly basis. Serve as lead writer for IA\u2019s Senior Vice President event remarks and oversee those for the President and other University leadership in connection with fundraising/donor-focused events. Help ensure that written materials adhere to the highest standards of quality, style, and accuracy. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree in English, Journalism, Communications or related field, or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 3 years of professional writing and editing experience. Excellent writing skills, including grammar, spelling, and proofreading. Demonstrated ability to handle confidential materials with discretion. Effective research skills and the capability to synthesize large quantities of information into clear, compelling narratives. Strong project management skills with the competence to manage multiple tasks and deadlines. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office programs, especially Excel. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a deadline-driven environment. Flexibility to adapt to shifting priorities and navigate ambiguity effectively. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends as necessary. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a higher education environment, particularly in a development or donor relations role. Familiarity with donor databases and communications platforms (e.g., Advance, ThankView). Expertise in writing on behalf of senior leadership of an organization. Knowledge of contemporary issues and methods in higher education institutional advancement and fundraising. Experience supporting fundraising writing. Location Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade K . Compensation for this grade ranges from $60,240 - $90,350 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. In addition, please submit 3 professional (non-academic) writing samples, such as a gift acknowledgement, a personalized impact/stewardship report, a tribute letter, newspaper article or other examples of business-focused material. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. #LI-Hybrid Apply Now First Name (required) e07ad8bc Last Name (required) dcd6eb48 Email (required) d26652ef Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 3dfa85e5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Institutional Advancement Drexel University Institutional Advancement Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 778ad727 Last Name (required) b2122d93 Email (required) 3727237d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/university-police-officer-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states-f6a575c3-7d71-4e40-a024-75687559b19c": {"title": "University Police Officer - University City", "description": "University Police Officer - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University Police Officer - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! University Police Officer 506576 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Drexel University Finance and Administration Full-Time Closing on: Oct 31 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Drexel University police officers are responsible for providing effective and accountable law enforcement services within a diverse educational environment. The primary functions of the Drexel University Police are the protection of life and property, preservation of the peace and responding to calls for service. These functions are accomplished through visible preventive patrol and the enforcement of city, state and federal laws and University regulations. This is a collective bargaining position governed by the Drexel Police Association agreement. Confidentiality Statement: All candidates must be willing to sign a confidentiality statement relating to the confidentiality of sensitive University information, student records, faculty records, staff records and all information deemed confidential by the Department of Public Safety and Drexel University. Essential Functions Utilizes \"best practices\" of modern community-oriented policing to prevent criminal activity and to enhance the quality of life for the community. Adheres to the highest ethical and professional standards in the Enforcement of Federal, State, City laws/ordinances and University regulations through patrol, investigations and the apprehension and prosecution of violators. Facilitates traffic safety by enforcing traffic laws and ordinances, investigating traffic accidents and regulating vehicular and pedestrian traffic. Mediates disputes for the purpose of preventing crime and maintaining the peace. Investigates criminal offenses and takes necessary steps to identify and arrest violators; testifies in criminal justice proceedings. Completes detailed reports and documentation essential to the effective operation of the Department and to support criminal and internal investigations. Provides police and customer services, first aid and general assistance as required. Promotes the concept of community by serving as public safety ambassador at university and public gatherings and by protecting the collective and individual rights of the community and its members. Interacts with various public and private groups and individuals to promote and explain the functions and responsibilities of the Department. Educates the public on security and traffic safety topics. Required to work varied shifts. Other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a HS Diploma or GED. Act 120 and PA MPOETC certified (a graduate of a Pennsylvania municipal police academy or a graduate of an out-of-state police academy program recognized by the Municipal Police Officers' Education and Training Commission). Must possess a valid Driver's License. Must be at least 21 years of age. Preferred Qualifications Associate degree preferred. Physical Demands Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Typically running, climbing Lifting demands \u2264 50lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This is a Full-Time Union position classified as Non-Exempt. Benefits and compensation are based on the agreed Collective Bargaining Agreement for this position. Candidates must agree to and satisfactorily pass (to be truthful, clear of, clean, and found not to have been convicted of any state or local laws) comprehensive background checks, including sensitive or confidential aspects of their personal lives. The background checks may include but are not limited to: education verification, past work history reference checks, vehicle operator license verification, past driving history, and a criminal records check. Vehicle operator license checks and criminal background checks will be conducted annually. The average background investigation takes one to two months. Because of the time needed for the background investigation, the average selection process can last up to six months. Applicants not elected may reapply whenever an opening for that specific position is available. Applicants who are disqualified during the pre-employment interview process or background investigation will only be reconsidered if the status of their eligibility has changed from the previous application. Applicants will be expected to show proof of current ACT 120 and PA MPOETC certifications during the interview process along with proof of a valid driver's license. Selection and Hiring Process: 1. The Drexel University Department of Human Resources and the Department of Public Safety (DPS) personnel develop a fully qualified applicant list. 2. Pre-employment interview(s) with DPS and other university representatives. 3. Comprehensive background investigation. 4. Conditional job offer (requires successful completion of physical examination which includes drug and alcohol screening & psychological evaluation to determine suitability for this position). 5. Candidates selected for employment are scheduled for orientation and in-service training. 6. Job will be posted for a minimum of 5 days. Background investigations are required for all new hires as a condition of employment, after the job offer is made. Employment may not begin until the University accepts the results of the background investigation. Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 77430740 Last Name (required) 768e8ecc Email (required) 3bc066ae Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 0012b0dd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Finance and Administration Drexel University Finance and Administration Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) f1d34933 Last Name (required) 7a7fd7da Email (required) 9740ea09 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/lab-assistant-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Lab Assistant - University City", "description": "Lab Assistant - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Lab Assistant - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Lab Assistant 507333 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions Full-Time Closing on: Oct 28 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary This is a full-time position in the College of Nursing & Health Professions supporting the Human Gross Anatomy Lab and anatomy instruction within the Health Sciences (HSCI) department. The position combines laboratory operations and instructional support with assigned teaching responsibilities in undergraduate Anatomy & Physiology (A&P) courses. The individual may also provide instructional support or teaching in graduate Physical Therapy (PT) or Physician Assistant (PA) courses, as assigned. Teaching responsibilities include guiding students through laboratory assignments, reinforcing anatomical concepts, and supporting a safe, organized, and effective learning environment. Essential Functions Perform job duties as requested by the Director of the Anatomy Lab as they relate to daily operations of the Human Gross Anatomy Lab and assigned teaching responsibilities. These include, but are not limited to: Lab Logistics Maintain all lab spaces in a \u201cReady State\u201d for teaching activities. Daily inspection of the lab to ensure housekeeping maintains a clean environment, including replacement of paper towels and soap, emptying trash, and cleaning sinks and floors. Maintain all anatomical specimens. Ensure specimens are covered/wrapped with wet toweling and stored on tables or in appropriate bins, closets, or assigned refrigerators. Inventory specimens and advise faculty on available specimens. Maintain compliance records for emergency eyewash and emergency shower. Maintain Chemical Tracker for all CNHP assigned labs. Manage biological waste and sharps disposal. Maintain appropriate signage in the lab. Assist with laboratory operations and supplies. Moving human donors between the laboratory and designated storage area and packaging them for removal. Supply inventory and ordering, including chemicals for cleaning and cadaver maintenance, miscellaneous cleaning supplies, PPE, tools, and office supplies for labs and exams. Maintain weekly inventory of disposable supplies and alert lab leadership of inventory needs. Assist with coordination of scheduling classes in the gross anatomy lab, including monitoring the lab calendar and communicating effectively with academic programs. Physical Therapy Physician Assistant Pathologists\u2019 Assistant Health Sciences Assist faculty with requested teaching support. Assist and/or lead teaching activities in all assigned labs. Preparation of identified structures on cadavers, specimens, joint preps and/or models. Set up and clean up materials used during each lab. Organize supplies, equipment, and teaching models/images in the lab spaces and supply closets. Dispose of outdated equipment, expired chemicals/supplies, and broken equipment. Monitor cooling units and report any issues. Coordinate timely disposal of unused cadaveric material as needed. Assist with 3D printing lab production of models. Teaching and Instructional Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate Anatomy & Physiology (A&P) laboratory sections within the Health Sciences (HSCI) department. Prepare the laboratory and instructional materials for lab sessions and ensure materials are returned, cleaned, and stored appropriately after instruction. Coordinate with other HSCI faculty regarding laboratory assignments, course schedules, learning objectives, instructional materials, and student needs. Participate in course-related meetings, instructional preparation, and other teaching activities necessary to fulfill assigned teaching responsibilities. As assigned and based on program needs and qualifications, provide teaching or instructional support in graduate Physical Therapy (PT) and/or Physician Assistant (PA) anatomy-related courses. Support Activities Assist Lab Leadership in recruiting, interviewing, hiring, training, scheduling, and providing day-to-day oversight of work-study assigned to the anatomy laboratory according to university procedures. Support high school and other outreach events involving the anatomy laboratory, including preparation, demonstrations, tours, and student engagement activities Assist with marketing and recruitment activities for undergraduate and graduate programs, including anatomy-related demonstrations, open houses, admitted-student events, and other program outreach activities as requested. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree in anatomy, anatomical sciences, anthropological sciences, a health-related field, or a related discipline with substantial coursework or experience in human anatomy or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 2+ years of experience Experience working with human cadaveric specimens and/or in a Human Gross Anatomy Lab. Experience teaching, facilitating, or providing instructional support to students in anatomy,. Demonstrated knowledge of human anatomy and the ability to effectively guide undergraduate students through A&P laboratory activities and assignments. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills appropriate for working with students, faculty, staff, and academic programs. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or higher in anatomy, anatomical sciences, anthropological sciences, a health-related field, or a related discipline with an emphasis in anatomy. Prior teaching experience in Anatomy & Physiology and/or related courses. Experience supporting cadaver-based instruction for health professions programs such as Physical Therapy or Physician Assistant education. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Lifting demands \u2264 25lbs Lifting demands > 50lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade I. Compensation for this grade ranges from $45,330 to $68,000 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) b8583ff6 Last Name (required) 4ad0f288 Email (required) 4ed3f940 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 4a560b80 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Nursing and Health Professions College of Nursing and Health Professions Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 485d5f7f Last Name (required) f8461904 Email (required) f9cfb726 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision 