t faculty life-cycle processes, including the Promotion & Tenure Process of tenure track and teaching faculty Assist with reports, if necessary Provide direction and advice to all employees, students, and vendors with business and academic operational questions. Resolve problems with the highest level of customer service Oversee select department-specific academic processes such as curriculum updates in Courseleaf and language placement exams Liaise and coordinate with the College scheduling team so that the team can ensure proper instructional assignments, course offerings, classroom spaces, etc. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 5 years of experience directly related to higher education, budget management, and/or customer service. Excellent computer skills including proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (including Microsoft Excel). Exceptional analytical skills and ability to oversee highly confidential information. Strong communication skills both written and verbal. Excellent attention to detail and multi-tasking skills. Exceptional customer services skills. Demonstrated commitment to follow-through of assigned tasks and projects. Ability to utilize critical thinking skills and judgment in problem-solving and decision-making, or escalating issues as needed. Strong interpersonal skills and collegiality. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade K. Compensation for this grade ranges from $60,240 - $90,350 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 62cedcf1 Last Name (required) 57f170a2 Email (required) 116a75b3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e2649ace Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences Drexel University College of Arts & Sciences Drexel University Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 7556e007 Last Name (required) 59d747d9 Email (required) 16e09107 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/adjunct-cnhp-undergrad-nursing-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Adjunct - CNHP - Undergrad Nursing - University City", "description": "Adjunct - CNHP - Undergrad Nursing - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Adjunct - CNHP - Undergrad Nursing - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Adjunct - CNHP - Undergrad Nursing 507389 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions Part-Time Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites About Drexel Drexel is a comprehensive global research university ranked among the top 100 in the nation. With over 24,000 students, Drexel is one of America's 15 largest private universities. Drexel is one of Philadelphia's top 10 private employers, and a major engine for economic development in the region. Drexel has committed to being the nation\u2019s most civically engaged university, with community partnerships integrated into every aspect of service and academics. Job Summary Drexel University's College of Nursing & Health Professions is the largest producer of RN's in the state of Pennsylvania. The College of Nursing and Health Professions has more than a century long history of educating nurses and health professionals. Since 2002, the College has embraced the practical ingenuity of Drexel through the refinement and development of more than 25 undergraduate and graduate nursing and health professions programs characterized by the integration of learning and work through cooperative education, a culture of excellence, innovation and technology infusion, research and deep civic engagement. The College uniquely prepares clinicians to practice and lead in a rapidly changing healthcare system. As a proven leader in Nursing Education, CNHP is seeking the best talent to further our profession and college's mission. These applications are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed by the Adjunct Faculty Coordinator when openings become available. Adjunct positions are contracted on a quarterly basis (four ten-week semesters). PLEASE NOTE: This posting does not guarantee a currently open position. Adjunct Nursing Faculty applications are being accepted for: 1. Undergraduate direct clinical supervision courses 2. Undergraduate classroom Essential Functions The adjunct faculty member will employ a variety of strategies to foster student learning and discussions, as well as, encourage active learning in all students, maintain proper course-related records, and evaluate student work and provide students with feedback as to the progress toward meeting the objectives of the course. Each adjunct faculty member is responsible for effectively teaching students in the assigned classroom, clinical, or laboratory settings. Each adjunct faculty member is responsible for effectively implementing the mission of the College of Nursing and Health Professions. Responsibilities may include teaching days, evenings, nights and weekends. Teach required number of credit hours per semester based on their contract Demonstrate knowledge and skills related to the teaching of adults, teaching methodology, curriculum development and evaluation. Assist in the design, implementation, and evaluation of the curriculum using a written plan. Plan and provide theoretical instruction and clinical or laboratory experiences that reflect an understanding of the philosophy, objectives and curriculum of the Nursing program and nursing profession. Evaluate student achievement of curricular objectives/outcomes related to nursing knowledge and practice. Schedule two office hours per week for student availability, if applicable. Schedule administrative time for classroom, laboratory, and clinical preparation. Maintain communication with the course chair and program chair regarding any course or student issues. Perform other similar duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree in Nursing. Hold a current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in the State of Pennsylvania. Progressive experience in nursing education and practice Current certification in CPR (clinical supervision) Current immunization as required (clinical supervision) PA Department of Public Welfare Child Abuse clearance; PA State Police Criminal Background clearance; FBI fingerprinting clearance (clinical supervision) Demonstrated competence with required knowledge and skill of assigned content area Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education and the role of Nurse Educator Ability to work collaboratively and effectively with other faculty members, as well as students. Excellent verbal, written, and electronic communication skills. Ability to perform the requirements of the job description (listed above). Basic computer skills including sending/receiving email; researching topics via the web; attaching, sending and opening documents; participation in chats; function in library databases. Current license and background checks may also be required in other states based upon the clinical location. Preferred Requirements Minimum of 1 year of experience Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. Apply Now First Name (required) d39d40fe Last Name (required) bfb5ea2f Email (required) 476c3775 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 538b9d23 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Nursing and Health Professions College of Nursing and Health Professions Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 13949919 Last Name (required) 520e389a Email (required) 3b4a9a0c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/director-alumni-programs-schools-colleges-hybrid-flexible-work-arrangement-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Director, Alumni Programs \u2013 Schools & Colleges", "description": "Director, Alumni Programs \u2013 Schools & Colleges - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Director, Alumni Programs \u2013 Schools & Colleges - Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Director, Alumni Programs \u2013 Schools & Colleges 507246 Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University Institutional Advancement Full-Time Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Director is responsible for providing leadership and oversight of alumni engagement initiatives for Drexel University's academic schools and colleges. They will develop and implement comprehensive engagement strategies that strengthen alumni relationships, increase volunteer participation, support fundraising and pipeline development efforts, and advance the goals of the Office of Institutional Advancement and the University. The Director works closely with deans, faculty, development officers, and administrative leaders to identify engagement priorities and develop meaningful opportunities that connect alumni to their academic home. This position supervises an Associate Director and Assistant Director and provides leadership for all school-and-college-based alumni engagement programs and initiatives. This is a hybrid position, working in person a few days a week. Essential Functions Develop and execute strategic engagement plans designed to strengthen alumni affinity, participation, volunteer involvement, professional networking, and philanthropic and student support. Serve as the primary Alumni and Constituent Engagement liaison to assigned schools and colleges. Meet regularly with deans, faculty, administrators, and development colleagues to identify opportunities for partnership. Identify opportunities to increase meaningful alumni engagement within assigned schools and colleges while aligning with Institutional Advancement objectives. Oversee planning and execution of school- and college-specific alumni events that support Dean\u2019s priorities, both virtual and in-person. Monitor effectiveness and make strategic recommendations for improvement. Partner closely with development colleagues to strengthen the alumni engagement pipeline and support fundraising priorities and campaign initiatives. Facilitate connections to maximize institutional impact. Collaborate on strategies that identify, cultivate, and engage alumni with the capacity and inclination for volunteer leadership and philanthropic support. Build relationships with alumni leaders and volunteers to support programming, mentorship, networking, advocacy, and philanthropic initiatives. Support alumni stewardship efforts through personalized and strategic outreach. Provide insights regarding alumni interests and participation. Track and analyze alumni engagement activities, volunteer participation, event attendance, and relationship management within the Advance database and other institutional systems. Supervise the Associate Director and Assistant Director of School and College Programs; Establish performance goals, provide professional development opportunities, and conduct regular check ins. Represent Alumni and Constituent Engagement at university and external events. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible experience in alumni relations, constituent engagement, volunteer management, advancement or higher education administration. Understanding of volunteer leadership structures and constituent engagement best practices. Demonstrated success in strategic program development and implementation. Experience working collaboratively with senior academic leaders, faculty, volunteers, and advancement professionals. Excellent project management, organizational, and leadership skills. Strong analytical skills and ability to utilize data to drive decision-making. Excellent written and verbal communication interpersonal skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and competing deadlines effectively. Ability and willingness to work evenings and weekends as required. Ability to represent Institutional Advancement effectively across the University. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in higher education or related field Experience supervising professional staff. Knowledge of fundraising and development principles. Location Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade M . Compensation for this grade ranges from $82,920 - $124,380 per year . Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. #LI-Hybrid Apply Now First Name (required) 7ea1a526 Last Name (required) ca652a4d Email (required) bdd2703b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert d304f772 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Institutional Advancement Drexel University Institutional Advancement Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 6185fbfc Last Name (required) 5e27d914 Email (required) 6dffad09 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-clinical-professor-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Assistant/Associate or Full Clinical Professor - University City", "description": "Assistant/Associate or Full Clinical Professor - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Assistant/Associate or Full Clinical Professor - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Assistant/Associate or Full Clinical Professor 507273 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions Full-Time Closing on: Dec 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Drexel University Physician Assistant (PA) Program invites applications from an experienced, energetic, and collaborative PA educator to join our faculty. This is a 12-month, non-tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Clinical Professor, Associate Clinical Professor, or Clinical Professor. The successful candidate will contribute to both the didactic and clinical phases of the program and will have opportunities to engage in teaching, student mentoring, assessment, curriculum development, and service. Drexel\u2019s PA Program is one of the nation\u2019s oldest and most established PA education programs. Located within the Drexel University College of Nursing & Health Professions (CNHP), the program prepares future physician assistants to provide high-quality, evidence-based, patient-centered care across diverse populations and clinical settings. We seek faculty who are committed to excellence in PA education, student success, interprofessional education, and the continued advancement of the PA profession. The College of Nursing & Health Professions is committed to increasing the diversity of our faculty, student body, and the physician assistant workforce. We value faculty who bring diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise to the classroom and clinical learning environment and who are committed to creating an inclusive and supportive educational experience for all students. In August 2022, CNHP moved to the newly constructed Health Sciences Building on Drexel\u2019s main campus in University City, Philadelphia. This state-of-the-art health education and research facility brings together CNHP\u2019s academic programs with Drexel\u2019s Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences & Professional Studies and College of Medicine, creating exceptional opportunities for collaboration across health professions and disciplines. The building provides modern instructional, simulation, clinical skills, research, and collaborative spaces that support innovative health professions education. Drexel\u2019s University City campus is situated within one of the nation\u2019s most dynamic academic and health sciences communities. The surrounding University City neighborhood is home to the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Medicine, Children\u2019s Hospital of Philadelphia, and numerous healthcare, research, technology, and life sciences organizations. The area is a vibrant hub for innovation, clinical practice, research, and education, with an extensive array of restaurants, businesses, cultural attractions, and wellness spaces. This is an exciting opportunity for a PA educator to join a well-established program within a comprehensive health professions college and to contribute to the education of the next generation of physician assistants. Essential Functions Collaborate with the Program Director, Associate Program Director, faculty, and staff to support excellence in PA education and student success across the didactic and clinical phases of the program. Contribute to the planning, implementation, and continuous improvement of curricular and programmatic initiatives. Participate in the development, review, and revision of the curriculum to ensure alignment with ARC-PA accreditation standards, the NCCPA Physician Assistant National Certifying Examination (PANCE) blueprint, and contemporary best practices in PA education. Serve as a course director and/or co-course director for assigned didactic and clinical courses. Develop and deliver engaging lectures, laboratory instruction, and other learning experiences based on established course objectives and student learning outcomes. Collaborate in course planning and design, including development and revision of instructional materials, assessments, learning activities, and other course resources. Participate in the assessment of student learning and progression, including ensuring that PA student competencies are appropriately assessed, documented, and monitored. Provide and/or coordinate remedial instruction and other academic support for students as appropriate. Serve as a faculty advisor to an assigned group of students across cohorts and mentor students regarding academic progress, professional development, and career preparation. Serve as a graduate project advisor for students within each cohort. Develop and maintain relationships with clinical education partners and identify new clinical sites to support the program's educational needs and growth. Participate in clinical education activities, including student site visits for clinical rotations and Primary Care Practicum experiences. Participate in the PA program's admissions process, including regular review of CASPA applications and participation in applicant interviews and selection activities. Participate in the ARC-PA accreditation process, including self-study preparation, continuous quality improvement activities, assessment, and implementation of accreditation-related initiatives. Engage in scholarly activity and contribute to research, presentations, publications, or other professional activities consistent with faculty expertise and interests. Serve on committees and participate in service activities at the program, college, and university levels. Represent the Drexel PA Program at local, state, and national professional meetings, conferences, and other activities that advance the program and the PA profession. Participate in PA program meetings, faculty retreats, student society activities, alumni events, white coat ceremonies, senior celebrations, and other program and college events. Contribute to the ongoing development and review of the PA Program's mission, goals, competencies, and strategic priorities. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Program Director. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master's Degree in Physician Assistant. Minimum of 1+ years of experience. Certified Physician Assistant with PA education experience Pennsylvania licensure or eligibility Excellence in classroom and/or clinical teaching Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and health equity Knowledge of and experience in the ARC-PA accreditation process Evidence of demonstrated commitment to student achievement and success as well as strong support for faculty development and a commitment to collaboration within the PA program and across the institution Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree (e.g., PhD, EdD, DMSc, DHSc) Evidence of successful and effective teaching in a physician assistant education program Evidence of demonstrated commitment to student success Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This is a Full-Time Faculty position classified as Exempt. The offered salary is based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Full-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet or Part-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet. Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 1bf6623b Last Name (required) 03a58a07 Email (required) 07a1b754 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 164781e6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Nursing and Health Professions College of Nursing and Health Professions Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 250ae572 Last Name (required) 12335f9a Email (required) 706698f8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/corporate-executive-education-part-time-business-development-director-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Corporate & Executive Education Part-Time Business Development Director - University City", "description": "Corporate & Executive Education Part-Time Business Development Director - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Corporate & Executive Education Part-Time Business Development Director - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Corporate & Executive Education Part-Time Business Development Director 507313 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Drexel University LeBow College of Business Part-Time Closing on: Oct 25 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Under the direction of the Executive Director of Corporate & Executive Education, the Part-Time Business Development Director will support revenue growth by identifying, developing, and advancing new corporate and organizational opportunities for executive education and customized learning solutions. The role will focus primarily on business development, relationship building, lead generation, and pipeline development, with an emphasis on identifying organizations with leadership development, talent development, AI, strategy, healthcare, and other executive education needs. The ideal candidate is a proactive, consultative business development professional who is comfortable engaging senior-level executives, identifying organizational needs, and developing relationships that can lead to new business opportunities. Essential Functions Business Development & Lead Generation: Identify and research prospective corporate, nonprofit, government, and industry clients aligned with Corporate & Executive Education priorities. Build and maintain a pipeline of qualified prospects using Salesforce and other business development tools. Conduct targeted outreach to prospective clients through email, phone, LinkedIn, networking, and other appropriate channels. Identify opportunities within priority industries, including healthcare, financial services, technology, manufacturing, pharma/life sciences, professional services, and government. Monitor industry trends, organizational priorities, and talent-development needs to identify potential opportunities for executive education. Generate introductions and meetings with decision-makers and influencers responsible for leadership development, talent, learning and development, strategy, and organizational transformation. Attend selected conferences, industry events, and networking opportunities to build relationships and identify prospects. Client Relationship Development: Develop and maintain relationships with current and prospective clients. Conduct initial discovery conversations to understand organizational goals, leadership challenges, talent priorities, and development needs. Identify opportunities for customized executive education, leadership development, executive programs, and other learning solutions. Maintain consistent follow-up with prospects and clients to advance opportunities through the business development process. Support post-program relationship development to identify opportunities for repeat business and expanded engagements. Opportunity Development: Qualify prospective opportunities based on organizational need, potential revenue, strategic fit, timing, and likelihood of conversion. Work with the Executive Director to translate client needs into potential program concepts and solutions. Collaborate with the Executive Director, faculty, and program team to develop proposals and presentations for qualified opportunities. Participate in client presentations and proposal discussions as appropriate. Support negotiations and the advancement of opportunities toward contract or engagement. CRM & Pipeline Management: Maintain accurate and timely records of prospects, contacts, activities, opportunities, and next steps in Salesforce. Provide regular updates on pipeline activity, prospect status, meetings, and emerging opportunities. Track business development activity and results, including qualified leads, meetings, proposals, and conversions. Use available market and business intelligence to identify opportunities and prioritize prospecting efforts. Collaboration: Work closely with the Executive Director to execute defined business development priorities and market strategies. Collaborate with Marketing and Communications to provide market intelligence and client insights that can inform messaging and outreach. Coordinate with program managers, faculty, academic partners, and other internal stakeholders as opportunities progress. Provide feedback on market demand, emerging client needs, competitive activity, and potential new program opportunities. The position may involve occasional attendance at industry events, client meetings, and Executive Education events outside of standard business hours. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a bachelor's degree in business, marketing, communications, sales, management, or a related field preferred or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 4 years or more of experience in business development, consultative sales, account management, executive education, leadership development, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to develop relationships and generate business in a B2B environment. Experience engaging senior executives and organizational decision-makers. Strong consultative selling and discovery skills. Excellent verbal, written, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to identify client needs and translate them into potential solutions. Strong organizational skills and ability to independently manage a pipeline and follow-up activities. Experience using Salesforce or another CRM system. Ability to conduct market research and identify potential clients and business opportunities. High emotional intelligence and strong relationship-building skills. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with university leadership, faculty, and internal teams. Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Non-Exempt, grade N . Compensation for this grade ranges from $47.76 - $71.64 per hour. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 4200deb2 Last Name (required) 8c773bec Email (required) 47d8800c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 762fb7bc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University LeBow College of Business Drexel University LeBow College of Business Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 03746a01 Last Name (required) c4d30fee Email (required) fb0965ac Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/research-associate-ii-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Research Associate II - University City", "description": "Research Associate II - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Research Associate II - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Research Associate II 507203 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Computing and Informatics College of Engineering Full-Time Closing on: Oct 22 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Drexel Wireless Systems Laboratory (DWSL) in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering seeks a highly motivated Research Associate to provide day-to-day technical leadership and help advance the laboratory's research, educational, and outreach activities. This position is ideal for an independent and collaborative researcher who enjoys developing new research directions, building experimental systems, mentoring students, and cultivating interdisciplinary partnerships. Working closely with the faculty director, the Research Associate will help translate broad research opportunities into focused projects, functioning prototypes, student research experiences, scholarly publications, and competitive proposals. The successful candidate will have meaningful opportunities to shape the laboratory's technical direction and to build a visible record of research leadership, mentorship, publication, and collaboration. The laboratory's research will be organized around three complementary themes: \u2022 Experimental wireless systems and platforms, including software-defined radio, RF systems, antennas, embedded platforms, testbeds, and reproducible wireless experimentation. \u2022 Intelligent wireless sensing and communications, including integrated sensing and communications, localization, AI-enabled wireless systems, edge intelligence, resilient networking, and digital twins for wireless experimentation. \u2022 Interdisciplinary RF and connected technologies, including wearable and fabric electronics, RF-enabled healthcare technologies, wireless sensors, and collaborative applications spanning engineering, computer science, and biomedical engineering. Candidates are not expected to have expertise in every area. Applicants with depth in one or more themes and an interest in working across disciplinary boundaries are encouraged to apply. The Research Associate will conduct hands-on research, guide undergraduate and graduate researchers, contribute to laboratory-based instruction, develop scholarly and proposal materials, and represent the laboratory through demonstrations, outreach activities, and collaborations with academic, government, and industrial partners. Essential Functions Research and Technical Leadership: Conduct independent and collaborative research within the laboratory's primary research themes. Identify focused and feasible research questions, develop research plans, and lead projects from initial concept through experimentation, analysis, and dissemination. Design, develop, evaluate, and integrate hardware and software platforms for experimental wireless research, including software-defined radios, embedded computing platforms, wireless sensors, RF instrumentation, simulation environments, and research software. Develop prototypes, preliminary results, reusable experimental capabilities, and other foundations for publications, collaborations, and future sponsored research. Remain current with emerging research trends and help identify promising directions that strengthen the laboratory's scholarly visibility and competitiveness for external funding. Establish sound practices for reproducible experimentation, technical documentation, software management, and research continuity. Student Mentoring and Team Development: Provide day-to-day technical guidance for undergraduate and graduate students working in the laboratory. Help students define achievable research questions, design experiments, analyze results, troubleshoot technical problems, and communicate their work effectively. Organize student project teams and establish a regular cadence of project planning, technical review, and feedback. Review student technical reports, publications, presentations, posters, demonstrations, and software or hardware deliverables. Develop onboarding materials and research practices that enable students to become productive contributors to the laboratory. Foster an inclusive, collaborative, safe, and intellectually engaging research environment. Research Development and Scholarly Communication. Contribute to peer-reviewed publications, conference papers, technical reports, invited presentations, demonstrations, and other scholarly outputs. Coordinate collaborative writing and help maintain steady progress from experimental results to publication. Identify relevant funding opportunities and contribute technical concepts, preliminary results, figures, project plans, and narrative material for proposals. Help develop new interdisciplinary research initiatives and cultivate productive relationships with academic, government, community, and industrial collaborators. Contribute to future sponsored projects as opportunities develop, including technical planning, execution, documentation, and communication of results. Educational Support: Support selected laboratory-intensive, simulation-based, and project-based courses within the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering. Develop or improve laboratory exercises, demonstrations, instructional materials, software examples, and experimental platforms related to the laboratory's technical areas. Assist students with wireless, embedded, RF, simulation, and software-development activities associated with laboratory or project-based learning. Participate, as appropriate, in selected instructional activities consistent with departmental needs and the terms of the appointment. Laboratory Infrastructure and Operations: Maintain a reliable, documented, and accessible experimental environment for student and faculty research. Support the effective use and routine care of software-defined radio platforms, RF measurement equipment, embedded systems, computing resources, research servers, and associated software. Maintain technical documentation, software repositories, equipment-use practices, and appropriate laboratory safety procedures. Recommend prioritized improvements to laboratory capabilities and coordinate technical implementation of approved upgrades. Outreach and Research Visibility: Develop and support compelling laboratory demonstrations, research showcases, campus events, and outreach activities. Help communicate the laboratory's work to prospective students, collaborators, sponsors, and broader audiences. Participate in activities involving K-12 students, educators, community partners, and other visitors, as appropriate. Represent the laboratory professionally in internal and external technical meetings and collaborative activities. Other Duties Perform other research, educational, laboratory, and outreach duties consistent with the scope of the position. Initial Areas of Emphasis During the initial appointment period, the Research Associate will work with the faculty director to: Establish a focused portfolio of technically feasible research initiatives aligned with the laboratory's primary themes. Develop experimental platforms, prototypes, preliminary results, and reusable research capabilities that support scholarly publication and future proposals. Establish effective structures for student onboarding, mentorship, project review, documentation, and research continuity. Strengthen the laboratory's pipeline of undergraduate and graduate research participation. Develop reusable instructional resources and demonstrations that connect the laboratory's research with education and outreach. Expand the laboratory's scholarly visibility and develop new interdisciplinary collaborations. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master's Degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a closely related field or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 1-2 years of experience. Exceptional candidates with an MS degree and substantial research and technical leadership experience may also be considered. Demonstrated research experience in wireless communications, RF systems, signal processing, networking, embedded systems, wireless sensing, or a related discipline. Strong programming experience using Python and at least one additional technical language or environment such as MATLAB or C++. Strong analytical, organizational, and technical writing skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work independently, set priorities, and translate broad objectives into concrete technical outcomes. Demonstrated ability or strong potential to mentor undergraduate or graduate student researchers. Ability to document technical processes, coordinate collaborative work, and follow projects through experimentation, analysis, and dissemination. Preferred Qualifications In one or more of the following areas: Software-defined radio and wireless prototyping Wireless communications and digital signal processing RF measurement and characterization Antenna design and testing Embedded systems, printed circuit board design, or IoT platforms Machine learning and artificial intelligence for wireless systems Wireless sensing, localization, or integrated sensing and communications Computer networking, distributed systems, or resilient wireless systems Linux-based research computing environments Containerized and reproducible computing environments Scientific writing and publication Technical proposal development Laboratory course development or instructional support Student research-team leadership Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 25lbs Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade K . Compensation for this grade ranges from $60,240.00 - $90,350.00 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 66296aef Last Name (required) 5236a5be Email (required) 14cb2bbf Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 77f4817d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Computing and Informatics College of Engineering College of Computing and Informatics College of Engineering Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) a81d0c84 Last Name (required) fd140b20 Email (required) 9bcf6e2c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/senior-technical-services-specialist-per-diem-salus-campus-elkins-park-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Senior Technical Services Specialist - Per diem - Salus Campus", "description": "Senior Technical Services Specialist - Per diem - Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Senior Technical Services Specialist - Per diem - Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Senior Technical Services Specialist - Per diem 507354 Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania Pennsylvania College of Optometry Part-Time Closing on: Oct 31 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Senior Technical Services Specialist (per diem) provides technical and administrative support to the Ophthalmic Repair Department and the Department of Technology Services This includes the installation, maintenance, operation, repair, and transportation of related equipment. The specialist also performs all functions related to the demonstration, sale, and maintenance of student medical equipment. This position is for training the new staff member. Key responsibilities include: Maintain and repair Optometric equipment Tracking student equipment orders and coordinating with vendors for pricing, receiving, and distribution. Working with the Senior EHR Analyst and the Finance department tracking student orders, sales, and sales tax. Mentoring repair technicians and assisting the Senior EHR Analyst with ordering parts, tools, and materials, including inventory control. Designing, engineering, and fabricating optical equipment, instruments, aids, and accessories. Coordinating the loaner instrument program and assisting in the sale and disposal of obsolete equipment. Essential Functions Collaborate with faculty to confirm required equipment. Order equipment for students in the OD & PA programs. Coordinate equipment distribution to students. Respond to student inquiries about their equipment. Manage equipment warranties, which involves contacting manufacturers and sending back broken or repairable items. Design, engineer, and fabricate optical equipment, instruments, low vision aids, teaching aids, research/development equipment, and computer accessories as needed. Repair, adjust, and clean optics. Calibrate, troubleshoot, and mechanically and electrically repair a wide variety of ophthalmic instruments, including both modern and obsolete models, such as keratometers, refractors, biomicroscopes, lensometers, acuity projectors, perimeters, radiuscopes, examination chairs and stands, indirect ophthalmoscopes, and microscopes. Maintain and operate all ophthalmic and audiovisual equipment at the University and satellite sites. Assist with supporting the University's automated ophthalmic equipment at EP, TEI, and remote Drexel satellite clinics. Assist with supporting audiovisual equipment in lab and classroom environments as required. Assist with the installation, configuration, troubleshooting, and repair of biomedical equipment, including M&S charts and other exam room and lab-specific equipment. Supervise and mentor ophthalmic technicians and students on machinery techniques, instrument maintenance procedures, room layouts, mirror system layouts, and low vision lens drilling. Work with the Senior EHR Analyst to contact vendors for pricing and availability of parts, bulbs, metals, woods, plastics, tools, and machine tools, and place orders. Solicit vendors for low bids on new ophthalmic equipment. Dispose of obsolete equipment. Coordinate the loaner instrument program with Drexel and instrument manufacturer's representatives and distribute equipment as necessary. Work with the Senior EHR Analyst to control the inventory of stock parts and instrument bulbs in the repair section, as well as stock of metals, plastic, nuts, bolts, and other supplies in the instrument shop. Manage inventory of equipment and its movement between satellite sites and the main campus and maintain inventory control for the business office. Work with the Senior EHR Analyst to manage departmental chargebacks for parts, bulbs, instrument covers, and materials used for equipment repair and project fabrication. Perform all other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Vocational or Technical School in or High School Diploma or GED Minimum of No minimum experience required - They will work with the current Senior Technical Services Specialist. Experience in design, engineering, and fabrication of optical and related equipment and instruments. Basic computer troubleshooting skills Supervisory experience and ability. Experience negotiating the purchase of equipment, materials, and supplies. Experience in inventory control. Familiarity with OSHA safety rules and regulations. Ability to represent the college professionally. Ability to lift and move large pieces of equipment safely. Physical Demands Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 50lbs Location Salus Campus - Elkins Park Additional Information This is a Part-Time per diem position classified as Non-Exempt. The offered pay is based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Per Diem/Casual/Temporary Benefit Fact Sheet . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 81418d9b Last Name (required) 6df22474 Email (required) 8dc1d35a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 629f1c81 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Pennsylvania College of Optometry Pennsylvania College of Optometry Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States Salus Campus - Elkins Park, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) a8a8ff94 Last Name (required) 0d815531 Email (required) cc1583d6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/open-rank-teaching-faculty-reading-campus-reading-pa-pennsylvania-united-states-ee0ff4a8-e457-46b5-87a4-a99f8f83a1e1": {"title": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty - Reading Campus", "description": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty - Reading Campus - Reading, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Open Rank Teaching Faculty - Reading Campus - Reading, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Open Rank Teaching Faculty 507296 Reading Campus - Reading, PA, Pennsylvania College of Medicine Part-Time Closing on: Dec 17 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Work with co-course directors to develop new content and cases for student learning when appropriate for the course. Work with co-course directors to teach small groups in the courses including history and physical exam sessions, biopsychosocial topic sessions and bioethics sessions. Assist in recruiting and developing additional faculty for small group sessions when needed in both FPC 2. Work with co-course directors in training selected standardized patients as Patient Instructors for clinical skills sessions. Prepare training materials for them to be able to teach our students in workshops and play their patient roles for histories and physicals. Be present for all focused history and physical exam sessions. Recruit and communicate with and train 4th years for the educational elective that partners with FPC2. Attend/provide training sessions for all 4th year elective activities. Oversee, facilitate and edit content for problem focused history and physical exam sessions. Work with co-course director to oversee all evaluations done by 4th years and faculty. Facilitate physical exam workshops including breast, pelvic and genitourinary exams. Will assist with other course responsibilities as necessary to ensure smooth operation of the course Will assist with editing and updating content for course website on Blackboard. Will attend appropriate meetings when possible including ECC 1, 2, Clinical skills working group and Course Directors meeting. Develop and facilitate interprofessional learning experiences Engage with faculty in different health professional schools to develop and implement learning experiences with a focus on the IPEC core competencies Identify, track and support students in academic difficulty within the course/thread. Maintain a scholarly focus in education. Assist with Simulation as needed Essential Functions Work with co-course directors to o develop new content and cases for student learning when appropriate for the course. Teach small groups in the courses including history and physical exam sessions, biopsychosocial topic sessions, interprofessional and bioethics sessions. Train selected standardized patients as Patient Instructors for clinical skills sessions. Prepare training materials for them to be able to teach our students in workshops and play their patient roles for histories and physicals. Recruit and developing additional faculty for small group sessions when needed in both FPC 2 campuses o Recruit, communicate with, and train 4th years for the educational elective that partners with FPC2. Attend/provide training sessions for all 4th year elective activities. Oversee all evaluations. Will attend educational meetings related to professional responsibilities. Identify, track, and support students in academic difficulty within the course/thread. Facilitate physical exam workshops including breast, pelvic and genitourinary exams (part of Clerkship Fundamentals- April) Facilitate small groups for physical exam, written documentation and oral presentation skills in Clerkship Fundamentals (April). Facilitate communication skills workshops in Transition to Clinician (March) Participates in Clinical Skills Assessment Delivery (March-April) Will serve as a clinical skills coach for students in phase 2 and 3 as needed. Participate in the interview process for the College of Medicine Required Qualifications Minimum of a Medical Doctor (MD) Minimum of At least five years\u2019 experience teaching in a graduate or medical education setting with evidence of effective teaching. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Demonstrated success in working well with faculty, administrators and students in an educational environment. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Location Reading Campus - Reading, PA Additional Information This is a Part-Time Faculty position classified as Exempt. The offered salary is based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Full-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet or Part-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet. Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 8060957e Last Name (required) 64e95107 Email (required) 0b7e246c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert abf12fae Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Medicine College of Medicine Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations Reading Campus - Reading, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Reading Campus - Reading, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 2118b5d6 Last Name (required) 6e8374e2 Email (required) 446a8fc3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/instructor-assistant-professor-the-eye-institute-oak-lane-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Instructor/Assistant Professor - The Eye Institute", "description": "Instructor/Assistant Professor - The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania, United States Instructor/Assistant Professor - The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Instructor/Assistant Professor 504960 The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania Pennsylvania College of Optometry Full-Time Closing on: Dec 31 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Provides clinical education/patient care within The Eye Institute (TEI) of Drexel University, including the flagship facility as well as the satellite clinical facilities. Within the didactic curriculum, provides instruction in preclinical skills and/or other laboratory/lecture roles as related to background, interests, and needs of the program. Essential Functions Provides clinical education to optometry students, residents and other personnel as assigned to the primary care (and specialty care services as appropriate) at TEI or its satellite facilities. Provides instruction in didactic, laboratory, small group education, and assessments to optometry students, based on the needs of the program. Provides feedback to students verbally during patient care, through daily patient encounter Meditrek log entries, to the chief of service for midterm and final evaluations, and attending grading meetings when appropriate. Assists the service chief in remediating struggling students as needed. Participates in clinical round tables before, during, or after clinical sessions. Participates in the education, mentoring, and evaluations of primary care and specialty care residents when appropriate. Participates with program directors and other faculty/staff in the planning, preparation, and implementation of integrated curricular content and clinical protocols based on the needs of the program. Participates in faculty meetings and engages in scholarly activity and provides service to the University, College, and profession. Participates in the Scholars Program as assigned. Responsible for accurate, timely medical record and Meditrek completion as well as compliance with the policies and procedures of the TEI Practice Manual and Drexel University. Performs other related duties as assigned. This clinical faculty appointment allows faculty to participate in the faculty promotion process, consistent with the current non-tenure track expectations. Required Qualifications Minimum of Doctor of Optometry Minimum of 1 year of residency or 4 years experience Graduation from an accredited school or college of optometry Current Pennsylvania license to practice optometry (with therapeutic and glaucoma privileges), or license-eligible Completion of a one-year or longer residency program in optometry, or a minimum of five years equivalent experience in clinical practice Eligible for faculty rank and professional staff appointment at TEI and PCO Continuing faculty appointment is contingent on maintaining clinical privileges consistent with TEI credentialing policies and protocols and adhering to established compliance protocols Preferred Qualifications Residency Prior supervisory experience in an optometric setting or at The Eye Institute Experience as an optometric educator Strong clinically- and educationally-related technology skills Demonstrated commitment to excellence in optometric education and patient care Demonstrated history of a positive work ethic FAAO - Fellow of the American Academy of Optometry Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Typically bending, crouching, stooping Typically running, climbing Location The Eye Institute - Oak Lane Additional Information This is a Full-Time Faculty position classified as Exempt. The offered salary is based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Full-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet or Part-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet. Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) e52f3ab8 Last Name (required) 6c80c86e Email (required) 98091ca9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 0784fd32 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Pennsylvania College of Optometry Pennsylvania College of Optometry Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania, United States The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) ea5e6867 Last Name (required) ad656732 Email (required) 3493a3f5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/research-assistant-queen-lane-campus-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Research Assistant - Queen Lane Campus", "description": "Research Assistant - Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Research Assistant - Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Research Assistant 507315 Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Medicine Full-Time Closing on: Oct 24 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary We are seeking a highly motivated individual with a BS degree in Biology, Neuroscience, or a related field who is interested in brain research and neuroscience. The successful candidate will contribute to studies investigating the neural circuit dynamics underlying learning, memory, and cognition. The candidate will gain hands-on experience with a range of experimental approaches, including optogenetics, in vivo electrophysiological recordings, and behavioral testing in mice. Responsibilities will include conducting and supporting validation experiments, performing surgical procedures, carrying out behavioral assays, analyzing preliminary data, and processing and evaluating histological tissue. Prior experience working with rodents, behavioral testing, and histological techniques is highly desirable. Programming and data analysis skills are a plus. The ideal candidate is enthusiastic about neuroscience research, eager to learn new experimental approaches, attentive to experimental detail, and able to work effectively both independently and collaboratively in a research environment. This position is grant-funded; employment is contingent upon the continued availability of those funds. Essential Functions Mouse behavioral testing & surgery Optogenetic experiments In vivo electrophysiological recording Processing and evaluation of histological tissue Data analysis Required Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor's Degree in or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of One year of experience, including undergraduate lab research Undergraduate research experience working with rodents, behavioral testing, and histological techniques is highly desirable. Programming and data analysis skills are a plus. The ideal candidate is enthusiastic about neuroscience research, eager to learn new experimental approaches, attentive to experimental detail, and able to work effectively both independently and collaboratively in a research environment. Preferred Qualifications Biology, Neuroscience - prior experience working with rodents, behavioral testing, and histological techniques is highly desirable. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically standing, walking Location Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Non-Exempt, grade F. Compensation for this grade ranges from $15 to $23.31 per hour. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. Additional Required Documents A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 236e912c Last Name (required) 70b6c555 Email (required) d3da5895 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 5fc1913b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Medicine College of Medicine Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Queen Lane Campus - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 43870005 Last Name (required) 6e11a8ec Email (required) 9082edb3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/adjunct-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states-3a9060fc-f845-4a11-924c-445943c22741": {"title": "Adjunct - University City", "description": "Adjunct - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Adjunct - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Adjunct 506407 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Dornsife School of Public Health Part-Time Closing on: Nov 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites About Drexel Drexel University fulfills its founder's vision of preparing each new generation of students for productive professional and civic lives while also focusing the University's collective expertise on solving society's greatest problems. Drexel is an academically comprehensive and globally engaged urban research university, dedicated to advancing knowledge and society and to providing every student with a valuable, rigorous, experiential, technology-infused education, enriched by the nation's premier cooperative education program. The Dana and David Dornsife School of Public Health was founded on the principle of health as a human right and the recognition of the importance of social justice as a means to achieve health for all. The Graduate School of Public Health is ranked 19th in the nation by U.S. News & World Report, and we are proud to be ranked first in the City of Philadelphia. As part of a top-tier comprehensive research university, students benefit from specialized research centers and cross-disciplinary collaborations within the University, the City of Philadelphia and throughout the world. Job Summary Multiple courses may be available for Academic Year 2025-2026 in the Department of Community Health & Prevention including courses in behavior and social change theories, community theory and health practice, health communication, measuring health outcomes, outcomes and impact evaluation, global health, public health ethics, and history of public health. These courses have been taught previously, so previously used syllabi and course materials are available. The adjunct faculty member will select course materials in accordance with the approved course description, foster active learning in all students, maintain proper course-related records, evaluate student work, and provide students with feedback. Courses that enroll 30 or more will usually have a teaching assistant. Some courses are online and asynchronous, others are in-person on Drexel\u2019s University City campus. The School of Public Health is on the quarter system and each course is ten weeks long, with three hours of instruction per week. The full calendar can be viewed at https://drexel.edu/provost/policies-calendars/academic-calendars/quarters-2022-2024/ Essential Functions Teach required number of credit hours per quarter Plan and provide instructional experiences that reflect an understanding of the philosophy, objectives, and curriculum of the program Provide instruction consistent with approved course descriptions Evaluate student achievement of curricular objectives/outcomes Maintain communication with the department chair and program director regarding any course or student issues Supervise a teaching assistant, if one is assigned to the course Perform other similar duties as assigned Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in public health, social sciences, medicine, bioethics, history of science, or related areas. Must have teaching experience at the graduate or undergraduate level. If applying for a course focusing on global issues, global expertise is necessary. Special Instructions to the Applicant Applications should consist of a brief cover letter indicating which Drexel courses are of interest and describing your qualifications to teach them, a CV, and a list of references. Letters of reference will be requested from candidates who are invited for an interview. Electronic submissions in PDF format are required. Review of applicants will be ongoing until all adjunct teaching positions are full. Apply Now First Name (required) 89478070 Last Name (required) b314807b Email (required) b640834f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 2090436f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Dornsife School of Public Health Dornsife School of Public Health Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) c058ed6b Last Name (required) 73c6fbef Email (required) 413ebead Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/can-advisor-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "CAN Advisor - University City", "description": "CAN Advisor - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States CAN Advisor - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! CAN Advisor 507028 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania Drexel University Enrollment Management and Student Success Full-Time Closing on: Nov 5 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The CAN Advisor will provide academic and social skills support to neurodivergent students including students with autism and other developmental or learning differences. The CAN Advisor will help students develop effective learning skills, study habits, time management strategies and workplace skills. The CAN Advisor will collaborate with the CAN Director to provide direct and indirect supports and resources for student success, independence, and self-advocacy. The successful candidate will help students set short-term and long-term goals, and monitor goal progress throughout the academic year. The CAN Advisor will respond to students experiencing academic difficulties and will develop academic interventions designed to improve their academic performance. This person will assist students in learning effective study skills that involve awareness of how to learn - knowing how to retain, organize, integrate, and apply information, problem-solving, and successfully balancing life in the process. Essential Functions Meet with students one-on-one on a weekly, biweekly, or monthly basis to develop and monitor proactive plans for ongoing academic, social and employment success. Assist with workshops, skills training, and courses specifically for CAN students. Maintain up-to-date and accurate records of student interactions. Assist with the peer-mentoring program as needed. Assist with the Neurodragons Student Organization as needed. Assist in promoting CAN on Drexel\u2019s campus to prospective and new students as needed. Assist with planning and convening on and off-campus activities such as the Autism at Work: University Series events, Faculty and Staff Education Series events and working employee breakfasts with the Steinbright Career Development Center (SCDC). Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master's Degree an applicable field or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 1 year of experience. Knowledge of and ability to apply ABA methods. Knowledge of psychoeducational/social and adaptive assessments and interpretation of results. Ability to exercise sound judgment and to maintain confidentiality. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with various departments. Cultural awareness and competency demonstrated by working with and/or understanding of individuals of diverse identities, including those with different levels of academic preparation, and varying abilities. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communications skills. Ability to work occasional weekends/evenings throughout the year to support events. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in Higher Education with students with disabilities Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade J. Compensation for this grade ranges from $52,360 - $78,530 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) aec74702 Last Name (required) 28ffdd08 Email (required) 90858ad5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 53a46551 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Drexel University Enrollment Management and Student Success Drexel University Enrollment Management and Student Success Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) f963613e Last Name (required) b2ef2ee0 Email (required) 04c0b0b1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/academic-coordinator-university-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Academic Coordinator - University City", "description": "Academic Coordinator - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Academic Coordinator - University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Academic Coordinator 506833 University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Medicine Full-Time Closing on: Oct 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Academic Coordinator provides administrative support for the Director of Women's Health Education Program by assisting with all scheduling, coordinating community and clinical sites for the Women's Health electives and scholars program, providing support for updating and creating new lectures and functioning as the primary contract for medical students interested in any Women's Health Elective or research programs. Essential Functions Coordinate Women's Health Seminar Series and Scholar Program. Assist in reports and grant preparation. Provide administrative support and coordination for medical student education and community engagement. Collaborate with all aspects of the Office of Community Health and Inclusive Excellence Provide curricular support. Other duties as Assigned (Please do not add to this field) Required Qualifications Minimum of a Associate's Degree in or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) Minimum of 2-3 Years of experience. Must be proficient in MS office, specifically word, Excel, publisher, and power point. Excellent typing, proofreading, and editing skills, ability to handle multiple working assignments/projects. Ability to learn and use new computer skills as necessary to meet curricular needs. Excellent library skills to perform literature searches and retrieve articles needed for the Pathway. Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Location University City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Non-Exempt, grade H . Compensation for this grade ranges from $18.89 to $28.33 per hour. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 9d003b33 Last Name (required) d839ba23 Email (required) bc36facb Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 225972e4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Medicine College of Medicine Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States University City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 75d87f92 Last Name (required) d0cc9c0f Email (required) 0b5d9290 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/advanced-practice-provider-center-city-philadelphia-pa-pennsylvania-united-states-10b23ba6-aadc-4c62-bcb8-467e2c7d7da6": {"title": "Advanced Practice Provider - Center City", "description": "Advanced Practice Provider - Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Advanced Practice Provider - Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Advanced Practice Provider 506908 Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania College of Medicine Full-Time Closing on: Oct 31 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary The Partnership Program at Drexel University is seeking an Advanced Practice Provider (Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant) (NP/PA) who will be responsible for providing direct patient care in Drexel University\u2019s Partnership Program located at 1427 Vine Street. This practitioner will provide independent patient evaluations for new patients as well as follow-up office visits. Clinical judgement is practiced independently within the scope of practice for a NP/PA with collaboration with physicians and other members of our multidisciplinary team regarding patient care and management issues, treatment plan, and medication ordering as needed. Essential Functions Have independently scheduled office hours with appropriate patient type Provide clinical support to patients seen in the Partnership Program including assisting with patient calls, medication orders and refills, and providing patient educational sessions. Perform history and physicals as needed with appropriate diagnostic tests and implementation of plan of care Develop a diagnosis and management plan based on observation, physical exam, and analysis of collected data. Counsel and educate patients and their family members as needed regarding evaluation and plan of treatment. Collaborate with an interdisciplinary healthcare team to ensure optimal patient outcomes. Collaborate with the Medical Director, Clinical Director, and other personnel regarding operational issues in the clinic. Document in the patient\u2019s electronic medical record all visits including the treatment plan for each patient at each visit. Ensure timely documentation that meets compliance standards, capturing essential patient information including history, presenting issues, physical exams, diagnoses, and treatment plans. Assist with triage, interviewing, and counselling of patients. Formulate patient problem list including medical diagnosis, physical exam, nursing needs, and health risk. Perform, order, and interpret results of laboratory and diagnostic tests. Request and utilize medical consultation when appropriate and initiate referrals based on patient needs. Review diagnostic study results promptly and communicate follow-up plans to patients. Address messages and inquiries through the Epic portal. Provide coverage for in-basket messages as needed. Provide on call coverage as assigned by Medical Director Participate in quality improvement projects to enhance patient access and outcomes Maintain national board certification, state licensure, and required continuing education. 80% of this role will be providing direct patient care (4 days per week) with 20% administrative time (1 day per week) Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master's Degree in or the equivalent combination of education and work experience. ( Please review the Equivalency Chart for additional information.) National Board Certification as a Primary/Family Care Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant License to practice as an NP/NP in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Minimum of 2 years experience as an NP/PA in a clinical environment Preferred Qualifications Experience working with diverse patient populations. Experience caring for people living with HIV preferred Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, patients, and program partners Demonstrated ability to carefully set priorities, meet deadlines, and manage time efficiently Excellent organizational skills and ability to follow-up and follow-through with strong attention to detail Must have excellent written and verbal communication skills; experience in PC use and mainstream software applications (i.e., Microsoft Word, Excel, or comparable MAC applications) and familiarity with an electronic medical record system. Current BLS certification Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Location Center City - Philadelphia, PA Additional Information This position is classified as Exempt, grade N. Compensation for this grade ranges from $99,720 - $149,580 per year. Please note that the offered rate for this position will vary based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. Applicants are encouraged to explore the Professional Staff salary structure and Compensation Guidelines & Policies for more details on Drexel\u2019s compensation framework. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Benefits Brochure . Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) d10c0619 Last Name (required) e41ae007 Email (required) c7fa2b0e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 838559dd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Medicine College of Medicine Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States Center City - Philadelphia, PA, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) bfa2e010 Last Name (required) 677962be Email (required) 7cbf2838 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.drexel.edu/jobs/instructor-assistant-clinical-professor-cornea-contact-lens-the-eye-institute-oak-lane-pennsylvania-united-states": {"title": "Instructor/Assistant Clinical Professor -Cornea/Contact Lens - The Eye Institute", "description": "Instructor/Assistant Clinical Professor -Cornea/Contact Lens - The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania, United States Instructor/Assistant Clinical Professor -Cornea/Contact Lens - The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania, United States Kiosk mode Work at Drexel! Instructor/Assistant Clinical Professor -Cornea/Contact Lens 505968 The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania Pennsylvania College of Optometry Full-Time Closing on: Dec 31 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary Provides clinical education and patient care at The Eye Institute (TEI) of Drexel University, including both the flagship location and satellite clinical facilities. Within the didactic curriculum, the faculty member contributes through lab and/or lecture instruction, based on their expertise, interests, and the needs of the program. This is non tenure track position. Essential Functions Provides clinical education to optometry students, residents, and others assigned to the Specialty, and the Primary Care Services at The Eye Institute (TEI) and its satellite facilities, during a weekly schedule based on the current needs of the program, which may include evenings and Saturdays. Provides independent direct patient care as needed. Provides timely, constructive feedback to students during patient care, through daily patient encounter entries in Meditrek, to the Chief of Service, and during attending grading meetings. Assists the service chiefs in remediating struggling students as needed. Participates in clinical round tables before, during, or after clinical sessions. Participates in the education, mentoring, and evaluations of TEI residents when appropriate. Participates and organizes workshops as needed. Provides instruction in preclinical skills or other labs with the possibility of other didactic assignments as appropriate, based on the needs of the program and interest of the faculty member. Participates with program directors and other faculty/staff in the planning, preparation, and implementation of integrated curricular content and clinical protocols. Participates in faculty meetings, workshops, and development activities as appropriate. Participates in the Scholars Program as assigned. Responsible for accurate, timely medical record and Meditrek completion as well as compliance with the policies and procedures of the TEI Practice Manual and Drexel University. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a PhD or Doctorate in Doctor of Optometry. Minimum of Residency or 4 years equivalent experience. Specialty contact lens experience Eligible for faculty rank and professional staff appointment at TEI and PCO Continuing faculty appointment is contingent on maintaining clinical privileges consistent with TEI credentialing policies and protocols and adhering to established compliance protocols Preferred Qualifications Experience 5 years preferred Licenses/Certifications: Fellow/Diplomate, American Academy of Optometry Physical Demands Typically sitting at a desk/table Typically bending, crouching, stooping Lifting demands \u2264 25lbs Location The Eye Institute - Oak Lane Additional Information This is a Full-Time Faculty position classified as Exempt. The offered salary is based on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, department budget, and an internal equity review. For information about benefits, please review Drexel\u2019s Full-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet or Part-Time Faculty Benefit Fact Sheet. Special Instructions to the Applicant Please make sure you upload your CV/resume and cover letter when submitting your application. A review of applicants will begin once a suitable candidate pool is identified. Apply Now First Name (required) 11f2febe Last Name (required) 74de98c3 Email (required) 97be3cde Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Post-Doctoral Research Position Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania College of Nursing and Health Professions The A.J. Drexel Autism Institute is seeking Post-Doctoral Research Fellow. Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Hybrid/Flexible Work Arrangement, Pennsylvania Drexel University, Kline School of Law Drexel University School of Law is seeking an Executive Director of Marketing and Communications Licensing Manager Remote, Pennsylvania Office of Research & Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation is seeking a Licensing Manager Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f3bb231e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Pennsylvania College of Optometry Pennsylvania College of Optometry Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania, United States The Eye Institute - Oak Lane, Pennsylvania, United States First Name (required) 023f073f Last Name (required) 8329ea9e Email (required) 72c09fd7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportuniti